arXiv:2509.15958v1 [cs.CL] 19 Sep 2025</div>
</div><div class="ltx_page_content">
<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line ltx_leqno">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Henri Cimetière
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_address"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Address: </span>Mathematical and Computer Engineering, Ecole Nationale des Ponts et Chaussées
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email address: </span><a href="mailto:henri.cimetiere@eleves.enpc.fr">henri.cimetiere@eleves.enpc.fr</a>
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">, </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Maria Teresa Chiri
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_address"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Address: </span>Department of Mathematics and Statistics, Queen’s University
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email address: </span><a href="mailto:maria.chiri@queensu.ca">maria.chiri@queensu.ca</a>
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before"> and </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Bahman Gharesifard
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_address"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Address: </span>Department of Mathematics and Statistics, Queen’s University
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email address: </span><a href="mailto:bahman.gharesifard@queensu.edu">bahman.gharesifard@queensu.edu</a>
</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract.</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce a new discrete-time attention model, termed the localmax dynamics, which interpolates between the classic softmax dynamics and the hardmax dynamics, where only the tokens that maximize the influence toward a given token have a positive weight. As in hardmax, uniform weights are determined by a parameter controlling neighbor influence, but the key extension lies in relaxing neighborhood interactions through an alignment-sensitivity parameter, which allows controlled deviations from pure hardmax behavior. As we prove, while the convex hull of the token states still converges to a convex polytope, its structure can no longer be fully described by a maximal alignment set, prompting the introduction of quiescent sets to capture the invariant behavior of tokens near vertices. We show that these sets play a key role in understanding the asymptotic behavior of the system, even under time-varying alignment sensitivity parameters. We further show that localmax dynamics does not exhibit finite-time convergence and provide results for vanishing, nonzero, time-varying alignment-sensitivity parameters, recovering the limiting behavior of hardmax as a by-product. Finally, we adapt Lyapunov-based methods from classical opinion dynamics, highlighting their limitations in the asymmetric setting of localmax interactions and outlining directions for future research.</p>
  
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1. </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The principle of attention was first introduced by Vaswani et al. in 2017 with the publication of their seminal work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>, which laid the foundation for the Transformer architecture. Transformers have enabled significant progress on tasks that were previously challenging for older neural network architectures. Today, they are widely applied across diverse domains, including natural language processing (e.g., ChatGPT, Google Translate, Grammarly), computer vision (e.g., object classification and detection), multilingual speech recognition, and many other areas. Despite their widespread use, our understanding of the internal structure and behavior of trained Transformers lags behind their practical successes. As an initial step toward bridging this gap, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite> establishes the expressive power of Transformer models by proving that they can universally approximate any continuous sequence-to-sequence function on a compact domain. In recent years, a growing body of work has sought to develop mathematical models that describe the dynamics of attention mechanisms. This line of inquiry was initiated in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>, which proposed the first interacting particle system to model Transformer dynamics. A simplified version of this model was later introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>, where the authors derived a continuous-time attention model based on the softmax function. The resulting dynamics are given by:</p>
<table id="S1.E1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S1.E1X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E1X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{x}_{i}(t)=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{e^{\langle Q(t)x_{i}(t),K(t)x_{j}(t)\rangle}}{\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{\langle Q(t)x_{i}(t),K(t)x_{k}(t)\rangle}}V(t)x_{j}(t)=\sum_{j=1}^{n}P_{ij}(t)V(t)x_{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{x}_{i}(t)=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{e^{\langle Q(t)x_{i}(t),K(t)x_{j}(t)\rangle}}{\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{\langle Q(t)x_{i}(t),K(t)x_{k}(t)\rangle}}V(t)x_{j}(t)=\sum_{j=1}^{n}P_{ij}(t)V(t)x_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> refers to the <math id="S1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th token<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
            
            
            
          We interchangeably use the wordings “token” and “particle” throughout the paper.</span></span></span> and the matrices <math id="S1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(t)</annotation></semantics></math> are, respectively, the query, the key and the value matrices at a given time <math id="S1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. The matrix <math id="S1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> with general term <math id="S1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{ij}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{ij}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is called the self-attention matrix. We will refer to this dynamic as the <span id="S1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> softmax</span> dynamics, since the weights in the derivative of the <math id="S1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th particle are given by the softmax function applied to the vector <math id="S1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\langle Qx_{i},Kx_{1}\rangle,\cdots,\langle Qx_{i},Kx_{n}\rangle\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\langle Qx_{i},Kx_{1}\rangle,\cdots,\langle Qx_{i},Kx_{n}\rangle\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>, the self-attention matrix is normalized using Sinkhorn’s
algorithm instead of the softmax operator in order to enforce a priori the doubly stochastic structure (i.e., a matrix whose rows and columns both sum to one) aspect on <math id="S1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>. This is motivated by the fact that the self-attention matrix in the softmax dynamics have been observed converge to a doubly stochastic matrix during the training process. On a similar note, it is observed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite> that the trained self-attention matrix is close to a low rank matrix, motivated their Transformers model called <span id="S1.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Linformers</span> re-designing the attention core to enforce a priori the low rank structure, leading the decreasing the global complexity of attention from <math id="S1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math>. In the same idea of dealing with the quadratic complexity of attention, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite> developed the <span id="S1.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">clustered attention</span> which consist in grouping “queries into clusters and computes attention just for the centroids”. This method somehow anticipates the clustering phenomenon that naturally occurs during the attention process, as we will study in this paper. More generally, a comprehensive classification of the different variants of Transformers is established in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>. Finally, it is worth pointing out that without skip connection, the self attention matrix converge with a doubly exponential rate to a rank one matrix, demonstrating the issue of rank collapse <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Going back to (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), following the literature, we will assume that the matrices <math id="S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> are independent from the layer <math id="S1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. This is justified in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>, where it is shown that the use of parameter-sharing across layers significantly reduce the number of parameters without seriously hurting performance. By studying the corresponding continuity equation, the authors in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> explain how the dynamics between particles can be seen as a flow map on measure spaces. The asymptotic behavior and the emergence of clusters for dynamics (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) has been studied by the same authors in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite> with various assumption on the matrices <math id="S1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>. In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, there is no layer normalization, however, the result presented is on a <span id="S1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">rescaled tokens</span> given by <math id="S1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}(t)=e^{-Vt}x_{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}(t)=e^{-Vt}x_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>, the layer normalization is made by projecting each token to the unit sphere, for some norm to be defined. In particular, for <math id="S1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\mathrm{Id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Id</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\mathrm{Id}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{T}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{T}K</annotation></semantics></math>
symmetric and positive defined, it has been shown in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite> that for any initial distribution, the rescaled tokens converge toward some points on the boundary of some convex polytope <math id="S1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Closely related to our work here, a simpler discrete-time dynamics is considered in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> with the constant value matrix <math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\alpha\mathrm{Id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Id</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\alpha\mathrm{Id}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Id</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Id}</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity matrix, for some parameter <math id="S1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. The layer normalization is made by dividing by a constant factor given by <math id="S1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. The dynamics is given by</p>
<table id="S1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{i}(t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{i}(t+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1+\alpha}\left(x_{i}(t)+\alpha\frac{1}{|C_{i}(t)|}\sum_{j\in C_{i}(t)}x_{j}(t)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1+\alpha}\left(x_{i}(t)+\alpha\frac{1}{|C_{i}(t)|}\sum_{j\in C_{i}(t)}x_{j}(t)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{i}(t)+\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}(t)|}\sum_{j\in C_{i}(t)}\left(x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{i}(t)+\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}(t)|}\sum_{j\in C_{i}(t)}\left(x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Here,</p>
<table id="S1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}(t)=\{j\in[n]\;|\;\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)\rangle=\max_{k\in[n]}\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{k}(t)\rangle\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}(t)=\{j\in[n]\;|\;\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)\rangle=\max_{k\in[n]}\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{k}(t)\rangle\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is a symmetric positive defined matrix parameterizing the transformer model, and is taken to be <math id="S1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=Q^{T}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=Q^{T}K</annotation></semantics></math>. To describe the intuition behind this model, note that the quantity of interest to determine if <math id="S1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> influences <math id="S1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle Ax_{i},x_{j}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle Ax_{i},x_{j}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, meaning that the greater this quantity is, the greater the influence of <math id="S1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is. The main difference between the two dynamics (apart from the discreet-time) is that in (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), the particles <math id="S1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> with low influence toward <math id="S1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> have a small positive weight whereas in (<a href="#S1.E2" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), only the particles that maximize the influence toward <math id="S1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> have a positive weight; we will refer to this second dynamics as <span id="S1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">hardmax dynamics.</span> In that sense, (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) can be seen as a regularization of (<a href="#S1.E2" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). The asymptotic behavior of particles following (2) has been studied in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>. In particular, it has been shown that there exists a convex polytope <math id="S1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that any <math id="S1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> converges to a vertex of <math id="S1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> or the projection of the origin onto some facet of <math id="S1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. The notion of <span id="S1.p4.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">leaders</span> (particles <math id="S1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}(t)=\{i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}(t)=\{i\}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>) is also introduced. This is a similar result to the one about dynamics (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), but the simplicity of the hardmax model allows for a more precise characterization of the structure of the limit points, see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, Theorem 1.1]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Related to our work below, and as already pointed out in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>, the attention models introduced above for Transformers are closely related to some opinion dynamics models, in particular, the Hegselmann-Krause (HK) dynamics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>. The clustering mechanism for this model has been studied in many references, including <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>. More specifically, under appropriate conditions, convergence to an opinion profile consisting of consensus subgroups has been established in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>. The fact that the HK dynamics terminate in finite time was shown in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>. Additionally, upper bounds on the termination time have been derived in both the one-dimensional and multi-dimensional settings in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Statement of contributions</h3>

<div id="S1.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce a new discrete-time model, termed as <em id="S1.SSx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">localmax dynamics</em>, which comparing to (<a href="#S1.E2" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) better mimics the
softmax dynamics (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). The key idea behind this model is to relax the notion of neighborhood (<a href="#S1.E3" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) by introducing an alignment sensitivity parameter, which can be designed and allows for deviations from the hard constraints in (<a href="#S1.E2" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) that only the particles that maximize the influence toward a token have a positive weights. Similar to what is known for (<a href="#S1.E2" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), we prove that under this new dynamics, the convex hull of the tokens’ states converges to a convex polytope. We define the notion of maximal alignment set as the state of points in this convex polytope aligned maximally with a vertex. After providing a precise characterization of this set, we show that for the localmax dynamics – in contrast to the hardmax and softmax dynamics – the structure of this convex polytope cannot be solely characterized by the maximal alignment set. Given this, and to gain insight into the behavior of the trajectories of the tokens in regions near the vertices of, we define the notion of
quiescent set and show that tokens in this set will become invariant with time. As an important by-product, we prove that the localmax dynamics we have introduced will never have finite time convergence. We also prove the convergence to the maximal alignement set in the regime where the alignment sensitivity parameter is time-varying, and approaches zero. Besides the fact that this recovers the known results on convergence of the hardmax dynamics to maximal alignment set, the result reveals non-trivial facts about the localmax dynamics with time-varying alignment sensitivity parameter. As our final contribution, we examine the Lyapunov analysis commonly employed in the study of Hegselmann-Krause dynamics, now in the context of localmax dynamics. In this setting, the Lyapunov function leverages the structure of the adjoint dynamics. While this approach yields useful insights into the behavior of the adjoint vector relative to neighborhood clusters, the inherent asymmetry in the localmax neighborhoods poses significant challenges to further progress using this method. We conclude by discussing these difficulties and outlining several open directions for future research.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2. </span>New dynamics and problem statement</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we aim to investigate the asymptotic behavior of the following discrete-time dynamics:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t+1)=x_{i}(t)+\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{j}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\left(x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t+1)=x_{i}(t)+\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{j}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\left(x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed positive parameters of the model,</p>
<table id="S2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}^{\delta}(t)=\{j\in[n]\;|\;\max_{k\in[n]}\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{k}(t)\rangle-\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)\rangle\leq\delta\lVert Ax_{i}(t)\rVert\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}^{\delta}(t)=\{j\in[n]\;|\;\max_{k\in[n]}\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{k}(t)\rangle-\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)\rangle\leq\delta\lVert Ax_{i}(t)\rVert\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">is the neighborhood of <math id="S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="S2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A\in\real^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\real^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a given symmetric positive matrix. We sometimes refer to the <math id="S2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> as the <em id="S2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">alignment sensitivity parameter</em>. As in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, we suppose <math id="S2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> to be time-independent, and will be taken to be <math id="S2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=Q^{T}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=Q^{T}K</annotation></semantics></math> for most parts of what follows. We begin by outlining the intuition behind this model and explaining its significance.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1. </span>Motivations</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, note that the dynamics followed by the rescaled tokens in (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) with <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\mathrm{Id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Id</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\mathrm{Id}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=Q^{T}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=Q^{T}K</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</p>
<table id="S2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{z}_{i}(t)=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{e^{e^{2t}\langle Az_{i}(t),z_{j}(t)\rangle}}{\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{e^{2t}\langle Az_{i}(t),z_{k}(t)\rangle}}\left(z_{j}(t)-z_{i}(t)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{z}_{i}(t)=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{e^{e^{2t}\langle Az_{i}(t),z_{j}(t)\rangle}}{\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{e^{2t}\langle Az_{i}(t),z_{k}(t)\rangle}}\left(z_{j}(t)-z_{i}(t)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We observe that a scaling factor <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{2t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{2t}</annotation></semantics></math> appears in front of the quantity <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle Az_{i}(t),z_{j}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle Az_{i}(t),z_{j}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. As a result, for <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> large, the only non-negligible weights are associated with particles <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> maximizing <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle Az_{i}(t),z_{j}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle Az_{i}(t),z_{j}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. This is similar to what happens in dynamics (<a href="#S1.E2" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) but, at the beginning (for <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> small), dynamics (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) is richer in the sense that it allows a wider range of movement for the particles. For instance, a particle satisfying <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{argmax}_{k\in[n]}\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{k}(t)\rangle=\{i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>argmax</mtext><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{argmax}_{k\in[n]}\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{k}(t)\rangle=\{i\}</annotation></semantics></math> will be stationary for dynamics (<a href="#S1.E2" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), in contrast to (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Clearly, limitations in capturing such behaviors impact the expressivity of the outputs generated by pure hardmax models. This motivates our model (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), which replaces the neighborhood definition (<a href="#S1.E3" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) with (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). We now discuss some consequences of this modification. To wit, let <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mbox{argmax}_{k\in[n]}\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{k}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>argmax</mtext><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mbox{argmax}_{k\in[n]}\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{k}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. Instead of selecting only the particles in <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{argmax}_{k\in[n]}\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{k}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>argmax</mtext><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{argmax}_{k\in[n]}\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{k}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, we also select those in the strip of width <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, orthogonal to <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and starting from <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, see Figure <a href="#S2.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 2.1. Motivations ‣ 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. For this reason, from this point on, we refer to (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) as the <em id="S2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">localmax dynamics</em>, highlighting its contrasts with the hardmax dynamic (<a href="#S1.E2" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). It is important to note that since <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant parameter, the dynamics have a different behavior asymptotically. In particular, the set of candidate convergence point identified in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> and in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> is no longer valid in our case. However, in Section <a href="#S5" title="5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we show that by slightly modified our model, we retrieve the convergence in <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">It is convenient to denote by</p>
<table id="S2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}(t):=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\max_{k\in[n]}\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{k}(t)\rangle-\langle Ax_{i}(t),x\rangle\leq\delta\lVert Ax_{i}(t)\rVert\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.447em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}(t):=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\max_{k\in[n]}\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{k}(t)\rangle-\langle Ax_{i}(t),x\rangle\leq\delta\lVert Ax_{i}(t)\rVert\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">such that <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)\iff x_{j}(t)\in Z_{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)\iff x_{j}(t)\in Z_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.
In Figure <a href="#S2.F2.sf3" title="In Figure 2 ‣ 2.1. Motivations ‣ 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(c)</span></a>, <a href="#S2.F2.sf1" title="In Figure 2 ‣ 2.1. Motivations ‣ 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(a)</span></a>, and <a href="#S2.F2.sf2" title="In Figure 2 ‣ 2.1. Motivations ‣ 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(b)</span></a>, we plot the trajectories for dynamics (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2.1. Motivations ‣ 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), (<a href="#S1.E2" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), and (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), respectively. We take a random initial distribution in the box <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]\times[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]\times[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and set the parameters <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0.3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{max}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{max}=100</annotation></semantics></math>. We also plot the initial and final convex hull of the tokens. We observe that the pure hardmax dynamics allows very little movement for the convex hull while tokens following the hardmax dynamics with strip of width <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> have a behavior that is more similar to the softmax dynamics.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.15958v1/C_delta_representation.png" id="S2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:527/275;" width="527" height="275" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1. </span>Representation of the set <math id="S2.F1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}^{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}^{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> (in green) in the case <math id="S2.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.F1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The two red lines correspond to the border of <math id="S2.F1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S2.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S2.F2.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.15958v1/pure_hardmax.png" id="S2.F2.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:198/148;" width="198" height="148" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F2.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S2.F2.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Pure hardmax dynamics</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S2.F2.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.15958v1/hardmax_delta.png" id="S2.F2.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:198/148;" width="198" height="148" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F2.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S2.F2.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Localmax dynamics with <math id="S2.F2.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0.3</annotation></semantics></math></span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S2.F2.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.15958v1/softmax.png" id="S2.F2.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:198/148;" width="198" height="148" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F2.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="S2.F2.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Softmax dynamics</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2. </span>Comparison between the trajectories for the different dynamics for the same random initial distribution (<math id="S2.F2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=30</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2</annotation></semantics></math>). The convex hull of the initial (resp. final) distribution is represented in red (resp. black).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 2.1</span></span><span id="S2.Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From now on, we will always take <math id="S2.Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is because we can easily recover the general case by changing the inner product, as <math id="S2.Thmremark1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is always assumed to be symmetric and positive defined.  <span id="S2.Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><math id="S2.Thmremark1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\diamond" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋄</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\diamond</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3. </span>Macro-level properties of the trajectories</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In what follows, <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i}(t))_{1\leq i\leq n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i}(t))_{1\leq i\leq n}</annotation></semantics></math> will always refer to the position of the tokens for an arbitrary initial distribution at time <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, which in turn defines the trajectories. Also, we will use the notation <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Conv}(x_{\ell}(t),1\leq\ell\leq n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Conv</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Conv}(x_{\ell}(t),1\leq\ell\leq n)</annotation></semantics></math> to refer to the convex hull of the particles at time <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Convergence of convex hull to a polytope):</span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">

The convex hull <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Conv}(x_{l}(t),1\leq\ell\leq n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Conv</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Conv}(x_{l}(t),1\leq\ell\leq n)</annotation></semantics></math> converges toward a convex polytope <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> be any closed half space of <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> that does not contain any <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐧</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be the unit outer normal to <math id="S3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mbox{argmin}_{i\in[n]}\,\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t),H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>argmin</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>dist</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mbox{argmin}_{i\in[n]}\,\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t),H)</annotation></semantics></math>, then any particle in <math id="S3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is further away from <math id="S3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> than <math id="S3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we have that</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{\ell}(t)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle\geq 0\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{\ell}(t)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle\geq 0\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">for any <math id="S3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in C_{j}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in C_{j}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that <math id="S3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{j}(t+1)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{j}(t+1)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, particles in <math id="S3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{argmin}_{i\in[n]}\,\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t),H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>argmin</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>dist</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{argmin}_{i\in[n]}\,\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t),H)</annotation></semantics></math> must get further away from <math id="S3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let us now take <math id="S3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]\backslash\mbox{argmin}_{\ell\in[n]}\,\mathrm{dist}(x_{\ell}(t),H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msub><mtext>argmin</mtext><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>dist</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]\backslash\mbox{argmin}_{\ell\in[n]}\,\mathrm{dist}(x_{\ell}(t),H)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since, <math id="S3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mbox{argmin}_{\ell\in[n]}\,\mathrm{dist}(x_{\ell}(t),H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>argmin</mtext><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>dist</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mbox{argmin}_{\ell\in[n]}\,\mathrm{dist}(x_{\ell}(t),H)</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that for any <math id="S3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{\ell}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle\geq\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{\ell}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle\geq\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we have that</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex3X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle x_{i}(t+1)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle x_{i}(t+1)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{{\ell}\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{\ell}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{{\ell}\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{\ell}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex3Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{{\ell}\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{{\ell}\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex3Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex3Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;-|\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle|\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;-|\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">This proves that</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t+1),H)&gt;\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),H)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t+1),H)&gt;\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),H)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the minimal distance between the particles and <math id="S3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> increases with <math id="S3.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, upon rewriting</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Conv}(x_{\ell}(t),1\leq\ell\leq n)=\bigcap_{\begin{subarray}{c}H\ \text{closed half space}\\
\mathrm{Conv}(x_{\ell}(t),\,1\leq{\ell}\leq n)\cap H=\emptyset\end{subarray}}\mathbb{R}^{d}\backslash H\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Conv</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.410em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>closed half space</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>Conv</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∩</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Conv}(x_{\ell}(t),1\leq\ell\leq n)=\bigcap_{\begin{subarray}{c}H\ \text{closed half space}\\
\mathrm{Conv}(x_{\ell}(t),\,1\leq{\ell}\leq n)\cap H=\emptyset\end{subarray}}\mathbb{R}^{d}\backslash H\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">it follows that <math id="S3.p2.m21" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Conv}(x_{\ell}(t+1),1\leq\ell\leq n)\subset\mathrm{Conv}(x_{\ell}(t),1\leq\ell\leq n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Conv</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi>Conv</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Conv}(x_{\ell}(t+1),1\leq\ell\leq n)\subset\mathrm{Conv}(x_{\ell}(t),1\leq\ell\leq n)</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">From now on, we denote the limiting convex polytope in Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> by <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, and its vertices by the set <math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V:=\{v_{1},...,v_{r}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V:=\{v_{1},...,v_{r}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive integer.
Since <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex polytope, any element <math id="S3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as a convex combination of the vertices of <math id="S3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> : There exist <math id="S3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1},....,\alpha_{r}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1},....,\alpha_{r}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{r}\alpha_{k}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{r}\alpha_{k}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\sum_{k=1}^{r}\alpha_{k}v_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\sum_{k=1}^{r}\alpha_{k}v_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, it is easy to see that <math id="S3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert x\rVert\leq\max_{k\in[r]}\langle x,v_{k}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert x\rVert\leq\max_{k\in[r]}\langle x,v_{k}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. For later use, we define</p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t):=\max_{k\in[n]}\mathrm{dist}(x_{k}(t),K)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t):=\max_{k\in[n]}\mathrm{dist}(x_{k}(t),K),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that by Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> implies that <math id="S3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\rightarrow+\infty}\eta(t)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\rightarrow+\infty}\eta(t)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Maximal alignment set):</span>
We define the following set of element in <math id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> :</p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S:=\{x\in K\;|\;\lVert x\rVert^{2}=\max_{k\in[r]}\langle x,v_{k}\rangle\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S:=\{x\in K\;|\;\lVert x\rVert^{2}=\max_{k\in[r]}\langle x,v_{k}\rangle\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and refer to it as the
<em id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">maximal alignment set</em>. We also define for any <math id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K</annotation></semantics></math> :</p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{x}:=\{\ell\in[r]\;|\;\langle x,v_{\ell}\rangle=\max_{k\in[r]}\langle x,v_{k}\rangle\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{x}:=\{\ell\in[r]\;|\;\langle x,v_{\ell}\rangle=\max_{k\in[r]}\langle x,v_{k}\rangle\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">As will be clear shortly, characterizing the maximal alignment set is closely related to understanding the structure of the limiting convex polytope. In fact, in the simpler dynamics considered in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, the trajectories of every particle eventually reaches this set. Notably, as will be discussed in more detail later, this is not the case for the localmax dynamics introduced in (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">It is worth pointing out here that even if the particles lie in <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, when we use the terminology of “border” or “hyperplane”, it will always be with respect to the smallest vector space <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="S3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This first lemma will play a crucial role in several arguments. Roughly speaking, it asserts that after a finite time, it is impossible for all particles located in a neighborhood of some vertex
<math id="S3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="S3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> to leave this neighborhood simultaneously at time <math id="S3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math>. From now on, for any <math id="S3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the notation <math id="S3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the set of points in <math id="S3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> that lie within distance at most <math id="S3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, that is:</p>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\epsilon}:=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\mathrm{dist}(x,K)\leq\epsilon\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\epsilon}:=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\mathrm{dist}(x,K)\leq\epsilon\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists an increasing sequence of time <math id="S3.Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{k})_{k\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{k})_{k\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> going to <math id="S3.Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for any <math id="S3.Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="S3.Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S3.Thmlemma1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t_{k})\in B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t_{k})\in B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmlemma1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t_{k}+1)\in B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t_{k}+1)\in B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q:=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\langle x-v,u\rangle=0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q:=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\langle x-v,u\rangle=0\}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is a unit vector such that <math id="S3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> supports <math id="S3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and in <math id="S3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> only, i.e.,
<math id="S3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subseteq\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\langle x-v,u\rangle\geq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subseteq\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\langle x-v,u\rangle\geq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\cap Q=\{v\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\cap Q=\{v\}</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists a constant <math id="S3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that if <math id="S3.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as in (<a href="#S3.E11" title="In 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), satisfies <math id="S3.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x-v,u\rangle\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x-v,u\rangle\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, we define the quantity</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mu}:=\inf_{y\in K_{\mu}\backslash B(v,\varepsilon)}\langle y-v,u\rangle\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mu}:=\inf_{y\in K_{\mu}\backslash B(v,\varepsilon)}\langle y-v,u\rangle\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Upon replacing <math id="S3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mu}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mu}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and using compactness of <math id="S3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> and the supporting property of <math id="S3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>,
we may assume that <math id="S3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mu}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mu}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
We now define <math id="S3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t)\leq\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t)\leq\mu</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because of the decrease of the convex hull for the inclusion, there exists at least one particle <math id="S3.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S3.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}(t)-v,u\rangle\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}(t)-v,u\rangle\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for any given time <math id="S3.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. This is equivalent to say that</span></p>
<table id="S3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(t):=\min_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{\ell}(t)-v,u\rangle\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(t):=\min_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{\ell}(t)-v,u\rangle\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Also, the convergence of the convex hull to <math id="S3.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="S3.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(t)\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(t)\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S3.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">We are now in position to conclude the proof. Suppose by contradiction that after finite time <math id="S3.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}\geq T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}\geq T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, all particles in <math id="S3.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="S3.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> will leave this set at time <math id="S3.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and take <math id="S3.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.p8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}(t+1)-v,u\rangle\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}(t+1)-v,u\rangle\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since, <math id="S3.p8.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that <math id="S3.p8.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t+1)\in B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t+1)\in B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> and since <math id="S3.p8.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that <math id="S3.p8.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in K_{\mu}\backslash B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in K_{\mu}\backslash B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>. Using (<a href="#S3.E13" title="In Proof. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>), we have that</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex6X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle x_{i}(t+1)-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle x_{i}(t+1)-</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex6X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{i}(t),u\rangle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),u\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{i}(t),u\rangle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),u\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex6Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\min_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{\ell}(t)-x_{i}(t),u\rangle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}m(t)+\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\langle v-x_{i}(t),u\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\min_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{\ell}(t)-x_{i}(t),u\rangle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}m(t)+\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\langle v-x_{i}(t),u\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E14.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle x_{i}(t+1)-v,u\rangle=\langle x_{i}(t+1)-v,u\rangle-\frac{1}{1+\alpha}\rho_{\mu}+\frac{1}{1+\alpha}\rho_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{i}(t+1)-v,u\rangle=\langle x_{i}(t+1)-v,u\rangle-\frac{1}{1+\alpha}\rho_{\mu}+\frac{1}{1+\alpha}\rho_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\langle x_{i}(t+1)-v,u\rangle-\frac{1}{1+\alpha}\langle v-x_{i}(t),u\rangle+\frac{1}{1+\alpha}\rho_{\mu}\geq\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}m(t)+\frac{1}{1+\alpha}\rho_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\langle x_{i}(t+1)-v,u\rangle-\frac{1}{1+\alpha}\langle v-x_{i}(t),u\rangle+\frac{1}{1+\alpha}\rho_{\mu}\geq\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}m(t)+\frac{1}{1+\alpha}\rho_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">It only remains to define <math id="S3.p8.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{3}\geq T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{3}\geq T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.p8.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|m(t)|&lt;\frac{\rho_{\mu}}{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|m(t)|&lt;\frac{\rho_{\mu}}{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.p8.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, for <math id="S3.p8.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S3.p8.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\notin B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\notin B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, then (<a href="#S3.E15" title="In Proof. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) simplifies to <math id="S3.p8.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}(t+1)-v,u\rangle&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}(t+1)-v,u\rangle&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">To summarize what we just proved: for <math id="S3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, we know by assumption that all the particles in <math id="S3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="S3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> will leave this set at time <math id="S3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, the particles outside <math id="S3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="S3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> cannot satisfy <math id="S3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}(t+1)-v,u\rangle\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}(t+1)-v,u\rangle\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
This proves that
no particle <em id="S3.p9.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">at all</em> can satisfy <math id="S3.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}(t+1)-v,u\rangle\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}(t+1)-v,u\rangle\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="S3.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a contradiction, because by definition (<a href="#S3.E13" title="In Proof. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>), <math id="S3.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(t)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(t)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S3.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> meaning that there always exists at least one index <math id="S3.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> for which</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}(t)-v,u\rangle\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}(t)-v,u\rangle\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p10.1" class="ltx_p">We still need a few intermediary results. Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, combined with Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, states that two particles located near two different vertex of <math id="S3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> cannot influence each other.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists a time <math id="S3.Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for any <math id="S3.Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="S3.Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v,v^{\prime}\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v,v^{\prime}\in V</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\neq v^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\neq v^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S3.Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\eta(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\eta(t))</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)\in B(v^{\prime},\eta(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)\in B(v^{\prime},\eta(t))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmlemma2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.Thmlemma2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t+1)\notin B(v,\eta(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t+1)\notin B(v,\eta(t))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose we can find <math id="S3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\eta(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\eta(t))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)\in B(v^{\prime},\eta(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)\in B(v^{\prime},\eta(t))</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that for the vertices of the polytope,
we can find <math id="S3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> unit vectors <math id="S3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="S3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq k,\ell\leq r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq k,\ell\leq r</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\neq l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\neq l</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v_{k},n_{k}\rangle&gt;\langle v_{\ell},n_{k}\rangle\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v_{k},n_{k}\rangle&gt;\langle v_{\ell},n_{k}\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S3.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> be the unit vector associated with <math id="S3.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote <math id="S3.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\langle v,n\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\langle v,n\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=\max_{k\in[r],v_{k}\neq v}\langle v_{k},n\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\max_{k\in[r],v_{k}\neq v}\langle v_{k},n\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and define <math id="S3.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\frac{s+S}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\frac{s+S}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\langle x,n\rangle=c\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\langle x,n\rangle=c\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We know that</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(v,H)=\min_{k\in[r],v_{k}\neq v}\mathrm{dist}(v_{k},H)=\frac{S-s}{2}:=D." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>:=</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(v,H)=\min_{k\in[r],v_{k}\neq v}\mathrm{dist}(v_{k},H)=\frac{S-s}{2}:=D.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then, the two following statements hold:</span></p>
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{\ell}(t)-x_{i}(t),n\rangle\leq 2\eta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{\ell}(t)-x_{i}(t),n\rangle\leq 2\eta(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),n\rangle&lt;-2(D-\eta(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),n\rangle&lt;-2(D-\eta(t))</annotation></semantics></math> as long as <math id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t)\leq D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t)\leq D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S3.p11.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p11.5.1" class="ltx_text">This is because all particles are at a distance of at most <math id="S3.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t)</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S3.p11.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S3.p11.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\eta(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\eta(t))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p11.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)\in B(v^{\prime},\eta(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)\in B(v^{\prime},\eta(t))</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="S3.E17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E17X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle x_{i}(t+1)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle x_{i}(t+1)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E17X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{k\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{k}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{k\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{k}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E17Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\left(2\eta(t)-2D+2(|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|-1)\eta(t)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\left(2\eta(t)-2D+2(|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|-1)\eta(t)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E17Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E17Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{2\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\left(|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|\eta(t)-D\right)\leq\frac{2\alpha}{1+\alpha}\left(\eta(t)-\frac{1}{n}D\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{2\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\left(|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|\eta(t)-D\right)\leq\frac{2\alpha}{1+\alpha}\left(\eta(t)-\frac{1}{n}D\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p11.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p11.6.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, we can define <math id="S3.p11.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.p11.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t)\leq\frac{\alpha}{1+2\alpha}\frac{D}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t)\leq\frac{\alpha}{1+2\alpha}\frac{D}{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.p11.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T</annotation></semantics></math> and state that if the previous setup holds for <math id="S3.p11.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.p11.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t+1)\notin B(v,\eta(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t+1)\notin B(v,\eta(t))</annotation></semantics></math>. We then conclude using Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Characterization of maximal alignment set):</span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">

The following properties hold true :</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The set </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is finite.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset\partial K\cup\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">⊂</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset\partial K\cup\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\subset S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\subset S</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The elements of </span><math id="S3.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> that are not in </span><math id="S3.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are the projection of the origin to some facet of </span><math id="S3.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of dimension </span><math id="S3.I2.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Before presenting the proof, we include some remarks to compare our results with those in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>. The proof of the first statement, item (1), is new, but the ones of item (2) and item (4) follow the same lines as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, Lemma 4.1 and Lemma 4.4]</cite>. However, crucially, the statement in item (3) is not proved in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, and the proof provided in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> for a different dynamics uses a strong convergence result that will not hold for our dynamics. In this sense, the proof we provide here is our main contribution to the characterization of the maximal alignment set <math id="S3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.
We begin with two general results that will be of great use in the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> as well as in subsequent arguments.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in K\backslash\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in K\backslash\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math>, recall that <math id="S3.Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{w}:=\mathrm{argmax}_{k\in[r]}\langle w,v_{k}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>argmax</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{w}:=\mathrm{argmax}_{k\in[r]}\langle w,v_{k}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S3.Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> the face of <math id="S3.Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> generated by the vertices in <math id="S3.Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists <math id="S3.Thmlemma3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmlemma3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="S3.Thmlemma3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> :</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\mathrm{dist}(y,F)\leq\varepsilon\mbox{ or }\|y-w\|\leq\varepsilon\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> or </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\mathrm{dist}(y,F)\leq\varepsilon\mbox{ or }\|y-w\|\leq\varepsilon\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{argmax}_{k\in[r]}\langle x,v_{k}\rangle\subset\mathcal{I}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>argmax</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{argmax}_{k\in[r]}\langle x,v_{k}\rangle\subset\mathcal{I}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any </span><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in B(w,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in B(w,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, if </span><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in K_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in K_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is such that </span><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(y,F)\geq 2\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(y,F)\geq 2\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x,y\rangle\leq\langle w,v_{j}\rangle-c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x,y\rangle\leq\langle w,v_{j}\rangle-c</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for any </span><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{I}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{I}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> be the function defined on <math id="S3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{j}(x)=\langle x,v_{j}\rangle-\max_{k\in[r]\backslash\mathcal{I}_{w}}\langle x,v_{k}\rangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{j}(x)=\langle x,v_{j}\rangle-\max_{k\in[r]\backslash\mathcal{I}_{w}}\langle x,v_{k}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">for any <math id="S3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{I}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{I}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>. This function is continuous and strictly positive on <math id="S3.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> but also satisfies <math id="S3.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(w)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(w)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, there exists <math id="S3.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="S3.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(x,F)\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(x,F)\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and for any <math id="S3.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in B(w,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in B(w,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>. This means that for any <math id="S3.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> close enough to <math id="S3.p13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\cup\{w\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\cup\{w\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the vertices maximizing the scalar product with <math id="S3.p13.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> are in <math id="S3.p13.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">Now, we know that :</span></p>
<table id="S3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left(y\in K_{\varepsilon}\;\;\mathrm{and}\;\;\mathrm{dist}(y,F)\geq 2\varepsilon\right)\implies\left(\forall y_{0}\in K,\;\|y-y_{0}\|\leq\varepsilon\implies\mathrm{dist}(y_{0},F)\geq\varepsilon\right)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mi>and</mi><mi>dist</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>ε</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>dist</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(y\in K_{\varepsilon}\;\;\mathrm{and}\;\;\mathrm{dist}(y,F)\geq 2\varepsilon\right)\implies\left(\forall y_{0}\in K,\;\|y-y_{0}\|\leq\varepsilon\implies\mathrm{dist}(y_{0},F)\geq\varepsilon\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p13.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p13.3.1" class="ltx_text">This is because <math id="S3.p13.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\varepsilon\leq\mathrm{dist}(y,F)\leq\mathrm{dist}(y_{0},F)+\|y-y_{0}\|\leq\mathrm{dist}(y_{0},F)+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\varepsilon\leq\mathrm{dist}(y,F)\leq\mathrm{dist}(y_{0},F)+\|y-y_{0}\|\leq\mathrm{dist}(y_{0},F)+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, we can define the mapping <math id="S3.p13.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto\sup_{z\in K,\mathrm{dist}(z,F)\geq\varepsilon}\langle x,z\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto\sup_{z\in K,\mathrm{dist}(z,F)\geq\varepsilon}\langle x,z\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p13.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p13.4.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="S3.p13.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous and satisfies <math id="S3.p13.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(w)\leq\langle w,v_{j}\rangle-c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(w)\leq\langle w,v_{j}\rangle-c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S3.p13.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and for any <math id="S3.p13.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{I}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{I}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is because <math id="S3.p13.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle w,\cdot\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle w,\cdot\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous, the set <math id="S3.p13.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{z\in K,\;\mathrm{dist}(z,F)\geq\varepsilon\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{z\in K,\;\mathrm{dist}(z,F)\geq\varepsilon\}</annotation></semantics></math> is compact, and <math id="S3.p13.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle w,\cdot\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle w,\cdot\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly less than <math id="S3.p13.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle w,v_{j}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle w,v_{j}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> on this set. Therefore, since any closed ball around <math id="S3.p13.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is compact, by continuity, we can define <math id="S3.p13.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that :</span></p>
<table id="S3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)\leq\langle w,v_{j}\rangle-\frac{c_{0}}{2},\;\;\mbox{for any}\;\;x\in B(w,\varepsilon_{2})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>for any</mtext><mo lspace="0.560em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)\leq\langle w,v_{j}\rangle-\frac{c_{0}}{2},\;\;\mbox{for any}\;\;x\in B(w,\varepsilon_{2})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p13.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p13.5.1" class="ltx_text">We are now in position to conclude the proof. Define <math id="S3.p13.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\leq\frac{c_{0}}{2(\max_{s\in K}\|s\|+\varepsilon)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\leq\frac{c_{0}}{2(\max_{s\in K}\|s\|+\varepsilon)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p13.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p13.6.1" class="ltx_text">for any <math id="S3.p13.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S3.p13.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}:=\min(\varepsilon_{1},\varepsilon_{2},\varepsilon_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}:=\min(\varepsilon_{1},\varepsilon_{2},\varepsilon_{3})</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S3.p13.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S3.p13.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in B(w,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in B(w,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<ul id="S3.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that <math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{argmax}_{k\in[r]}\langle x,v_{k}\rangle\subset\mathcal{I}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>argmax</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{argmax}_{k\in[r]}\langle x,v_{k}\rangle\subset\mathcal{I}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in K_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in K_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(y,F)\geq 2\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(y,F)\geq 2\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{0}\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{0}\in K</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|y-y_{0}\|\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|y-y_{0}\|\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Using (<a href="#S3.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>), we know that <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(y_{0},F)\geq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(y_{0},F)\geq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, using (<a href="#S3.E19" title="In Proof. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>), if <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{I}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{I}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x,y_{0}\rangle\leq\langle w,v_{j}\rangle-\frac{c_{0}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x,y_{0}\rangle\leq\langle w,v_{j}\rangle-\frac{c_{0}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then :</p>
<table id="S3.Ex12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex12X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle x,y\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle x,y\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle x,y_{0}\rangle+\langle x,y-y_{0}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle x,y_{0}\rangle+\langle x,y-y_{0}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex12Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\langle w,v_{j}\rangle-\frac{c_{0}}{2}+(\|w\|+\varepsilon)\varepsilon\leq\langle w,v_{j}\rangle-c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\langle w,v_{j}\rangle-\frac{c_{0}}{2}+(\|w\|+\varepsilon)\varepsilon\leq\langle w,v_{j}\rangle-c</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I4.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{c_{0}}{2}-(\|w\|+\varepsilon)\varepsilon\geq\frac{c_{0}}{2}-(\max_{s\in K}\|s\|+\varepsilon_{3})\varepsilon_{3}:=c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{c_{0}}{2}-(\|w\|+\varepsilon)\varepsilon\geq\frac{c_{0}}{2}-(\max_{s\in K}\|s\|+\varepsilon_{3})\varepsilon_{3}:=c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S3.p13.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p13.7.1" class="ltx_text">This concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.4</span></span><span id="S3.Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="S3.Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\max_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle-\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle x_{i}(t),v_{\ell}\rangle\leq\eta(t)\lVert x_{i}(t)\rVert\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\max_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle-\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle x_{i}(t),v_{\ell}\rangle\leq\eta(t)\lVert x_{i}(t)\rVert\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmlemma4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmlemma4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S3.Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is as in (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">The left inequality is obvious since <math id="S3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subset\mathrm{Conv}(x_{\ell},\ell\in[n])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>Conv</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subset\mathrm{Conv}(x_{\ell},\ell\in[n])</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, take <math id="S3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle=\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle=\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and suppose that <math id="S3.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)-v_{\ell}\rangle&gt;\eta(t)\lVert x_{i}(t)\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)-v_{\ell}\rangle&gt;\eta(t)\lVert x_{i}(t)\rVert</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq\ell\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq\ell\leq m</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="S3.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\sum_{\ell\in[r]}\alpha_{\ell}v_{\ell}\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\sum_{\ell\in[r]}\alpha_{\ell}v_{\ell}\in K</annotation></semantics></math>, we have :</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert x_{i}(t)\rVert\lVert x_{j}(t)-z\rVert\geq\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)-z\rangle=\sum_{\ell\in[r]}\alpha_{\ell}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)-v_{\ell}\rangle&gt;\eta(t)\lVert x_{i}(t)\rVert" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert x_{i}(t)\rVert\lVert x_{j}(t)-z\rVert\geq\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)-z\rangle=\sum_{\ell\in[r]}\alpha_{\ell}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)-v_{\ell}\rangle&gt;\eta(t)\lVert x_{i}(t)\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">which proves <math id="S3.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),K)&gt;\eta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),K)&gt;\eta(t)</annotation></semantics></math> which is not true by definition. This concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p15.1" class="ltx_p">We are now in a position to provide the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S3.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">We proceed with the proof of each item:</span></p>
<ul id="S3.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I5.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I5.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I5.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is a subset of <math id="S3.I5.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[r]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[r]</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, if we prove that</p>
<table id="S3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{x}={\mathcal{I}}_{y}\implies x=y," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{x}={\mathcal{I}}_{y}\implies x=y,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I5.ix1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">we have proved that <math id="S3.I5.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S|\leq 2^{m}&lt;+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S|\leq 2^{m}&lt;+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. To show this, let <math id="S3.I5.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in S</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.I5.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{x}={\mathcal{I}}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{x}={\mathcal{I}}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Writing <math id="S3.I5.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\sum_{k\in{\mathcal{I}}_{x}}\alpha_{k}v_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\sum_{k\in{\mathcal{I}}_{x}}\alpha_{k}v_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I5.ix1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\sum_{\ell\in{\mathcal{I}}_{y}}\alpha_{\ell}v_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\sum_{\ell\in{\mathcal{I}}_{y}}\alpha_{\ell}v_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> as convex combinations, we have that</p>
<table id="S3.Ex16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex16X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert x-y\rVert^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert x-y\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex16X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle x-y,x-y\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle x-y,x-y\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex16Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle x-\sum_{\ell\in{\mathcal{I}}_{y}}\beta_{\ell}v_{\ell},x\rangle-\langle\sum_{k\in{\mathcal{I}}_{x}}\alpha_{k}v_{k}-y,y\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle x-\sum_{\ell\in{\mathcal{I}}_{y}}\beta_{\ell}v_{\ell},x\rangle-\langle\sum_{k\in{\mathcal{I}}_{x}}\alpha_{k}v_{k}-y,y\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex16Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex16Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\ell\in I_{y}}\beta_{l}\langle x-v_{l},x\rangle-\sum_{k\in I_{x}}\alpha_{k}\langle v_{k}-y,y\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\ell\in I_{y}}\beta_{l}\langle x-v_{l},x\rangle-\sum_{k\in I_{x}}\alpha_{k}\langle v_{k}-y,y\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex16Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex16Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I5.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We proceed as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>. Let <math id="S3.I5.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in S</annotation></semantics></math>. We have</p>
<table id="S3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x,x\rangle=\max_{k\in[r]}\,\langle x,v_{k}\rangle=\max_{y\in K}\,\langle x,y\rangle," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x,x\rangle=\max_{k\in[r]}\,\langle x,v_{k}\rangle=\max_{y\in K}\,\langle x,y\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I5.ix2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which implies that <math id="S3.I5.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> maximizes the linear function <math id="S3.I5.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\mapsto\langle x,y\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\mapsto\langle x,y\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> on the convex polytope <math id="S3.I5.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves that <math id="S3.I5.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\partial K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\partial K</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S3.I5.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math> and suppose, on the contrary to the statement, that <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\notin S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\notin S</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J=\mathrm{argmax}_{k\in[r]}\langle v,v_{k}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>argmax</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J=\mathrm{argmax}_{k\in[r]}\langle v,v_{k}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. By assumption, <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{j}\neq v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{j}\neq v</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in J</annotation></semantics></math> which implies in particular that <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, take <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> with <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=v</annotation></semantics></math> and take <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. As stated by this lemma, we know that there exists <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in K_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in K_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is such that <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(y,F)\geq 2\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(y,F)\geq 2\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x,y\rangle\leq\langle w,v_{k}\rangle-c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x,y\rangle\leq\langle w,v_{k}\rangle-c</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in J</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since the convex hull <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Conv}(x_{\ell}(t),\ell\in[n])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Conv</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Conv}(x_{\ell}(t),\ell\in[n])</annotation></semantics></math> converges towards <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a particle in the <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t)-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t)-</annotation></semantics></math>neighborhood of any vertex for any given time <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> be such that for any <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t)\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t)\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. We fix <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and we take <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathrm{argmax}_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>argmax</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathrm{argmax}_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. Using Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 3.4. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)\rangle\geq\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle x_{i}(t),v_{\ell}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)\rangle\geq\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle x_{i}(t),v_{\ell}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies:</p>
<table id="S3.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(20)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)\rangle\geq\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle v,v_{\ell}\rangle-\varepsilon\max_{\ell\in[r]}\|v_{\ell}\|\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)\rangle\geq\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle v,v_{\ell}\rangle-\varepsilon\max_{\ell\in[r]}\|v_{\ell}\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\ell\in[r]}\|v_{\ell}\|&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\ell\in[r]}\|v_{\ell}\|&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> so, upon diminishing <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> (which amount to increasing <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>), we can also enforce the condition</p>
<table id="S3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\frac{c}{2\max_{\ell\in[r]}\|v_{\ell}\|}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\frac{c}{2\max_{\ell\in[r]}\|v_{\ell}\|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which, using (<a href="#S3.E20" title="In item (3) ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>), finally gives</p>
<table id="S3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)\rangle&gt;\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle v,v_{\ell}\rangle-c" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)\rangle&gt;\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle v,v_{\ell}\rangle-c</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and item (2) of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> gives that <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),F)\leq 2\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),F)\leq 2\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
By assumption, <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\notin F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\notin F</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|p_{F}(v)-v\|&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|p_{F}(v)-v\|&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is the orthogonal projection to <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{n}=\frac{p_{F}(v)-v}{\|p_{F}(v)-v\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{n}=\frac{p_{F}(v)-v}{\|p_{F}(v)-v\|}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathrm{argmax}_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>argmax</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathrm{argmax}_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. We write :</p>
<table id="S3.Ex20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex20X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex20X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle p_{F}(v)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle p_{F}(v)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex20X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle p_{F}(v)-p_{F}(x_{j}(t))+p_{F}(x_{j}(t))-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle p_{F}(v)-p_{F}(x_{j}(t))+p_{F}(x_{j}(t))-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex20Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex20Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle p_{F}(x_{j}(t))-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle p_{F}(x_{j}(t))-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex20Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex20Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|p_{F}(x_{j}(t))-x_{j}(t)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|p_{F}(x_{j}(t))-x_{j}(t)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex20Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex20Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),F)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex20Xd"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex20Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">and then:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex21X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex21X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex21X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle p_{F}(v)-v-(p_{F}(v)-x_{j}(t))+(v-x_{i}(t)),\mathbf{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle p_{F}(v)-v-(p_{F}(v)-x_{j}(t))+(v-x_{i}(t)),\mathbf{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex21Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex21Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle p_{F}(v)-v,\mathbf{n}\rangle-\langle p_{F}(v)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle+\langle v-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle p_{F}(v)-v,\mathbf{n}\rangle-\langle p_{F}(v)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle+\langle v-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex21Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex21Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\langle p_{F}(v)-v,\mathbf{n}\rangle-2\varepsilon-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\langle p_{F}(v)-v,\mathbf{n}\rangle-2\varepsilon-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex21Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex21Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|p_{F}(v)-v\|-3\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|p_{F}(v)-v\|-3\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">and also :</p>
<table id="S3.Ex22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex22X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex22X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|x_{i}(t+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|x_{i}(t+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex22X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1)-x_{i}(t)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1)-x_{i}(t)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex22Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex22Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\langle x_{i}(t+1)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\langle x_{i}(t+1)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex22Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex22Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{\ell\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{\ell}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{\ell\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{\ell}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex22Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex22Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\left(\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle+\sum_{\ell\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)\backslash\{j\}}\langle x_{\ell}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\left(\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle+\sum_{\ell\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)\backslash\{j\}}\langle x_{\ell}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Now, note that, since <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is a vertex of <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H:=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\langle x-v,\mathbf{n}\rangle\leq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H:=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\langle x-v,\mathbf{n}\rangle\leq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a half space supporting <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, if <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in K_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in K_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle y-v,\mathbf{n}\rangle\geq-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle y-v,\mathbf{n}\rangle\geq-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, which in turn implies that <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{\ell}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle\geq-2\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{\ell}(t)-x_{i}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle\geq-2\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining the two preceding inequalities, we conclude that</p>
<table id="S3.E21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E21X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(21)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E21X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|x_{i}(t+1)-x_{i}(t)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|x_{i}(t+1)-x_{i}(t)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E21X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\left(\|p_{F}(v)-v\|-3\varepsilon-2(|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|-1)\varepsilon\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\left(\|p_{F}(v)-v\|-3\varepsilon-2(|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|-1)\varepsilon\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E21Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E21Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\left(\frac{\|p_{F}(v)-v\|}{n}-3\varepsilon\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\left(\frac{\|p_{F}(v)-v\|}{n}-3\varepsilon\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.8" class="ltx_p">Recall that this is true as long as <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t)\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t)\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> i.e., <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we can take <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&lt;\frac{\|v-p_{F}(v)\|}{n}\frac{\alpha}{5\alpha+2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&lt;\frac{\|v-p_{F}(v)\|}{n}\frac{\alpha}{5\alpha+2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.9" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m53" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> depends on <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m54" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> so diminishing <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m55" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> amount to increasing <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m56" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We deduce that for <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m57" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m58" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(t+1)-x_{i}(t)\|\geq 2\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(t+1)-x_{i}(t)\|\geq 2\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> which proves that <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m59" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t+1)\notin B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t+1)\notin B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>. This is true for any particle located in <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m60" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m61" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves that after time <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m62" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m63" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t+1)\in B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t+1)\in B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.I5.ix3.p1.m64" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\notin B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\notin B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>. We then conclude using Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof follows exactly as the one in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, Lemma 4.4]</cite> and is omitted.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S3.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p17.1" class="ltx_p">The upshot of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> is that it provides a characterization for the maximal alignment set <math id="S3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. We make an important remark on the relationship between the maximal alignment set and the <math id="S3.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>-limit set of the dynamics (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="S3.Thmremark1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Convergence can happen outside the maximal alignment set):</span>

In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, the set <math id="S3.Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is of interest, because it corresponds exactly to candidate set of convergence point, in that every particle converges to some point in <math id="S3.Thmremark1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. This is not true for the dynamics (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). We illustrate this with an example. Consider the following configuration</p>
<ul id="S3.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One particle in <math id="S3.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}=(-10,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}=(-10,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, one in <math id="S3.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{2}=(11,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{2}=(11,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and one in <math id="S3.I6.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{3}=(0,-15)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{3}=(0,-15)</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Nine distinct particles randomly chosen in the square centered in <math id="S3.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O=(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O=(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> with length <math id="S3.I6.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One particle in <math id="S3.I6.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=(-0.9,1.1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=(-0.9,1.1)</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I6.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I6.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I6.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I6.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=8</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S3.Thmremark1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> is an illustration of this configuration<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
            Indeed, this numerical observation can easily be verified analytically.</span></span></span>.
This situation is of interest because it shows that it is possible for tokens to converge to points that are not in <math id="S3.Thmremark1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> (not a vertex nor the projection of the origin to some face of <math id="S3.Thmremark1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, this is figure <a href="#S3.F3.sf2" title="In Figure 3 ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(b)</span></a>) in the non-trivial case (initial distribution not at equilibrium). In fact, this is the fact that <math id="S3.Thmremark1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> is constant that allows convergence outside of <math id="S3.Thmremark1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, we can see that when we replace the constant <math id="S3.Thmremark1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> by a sequence <math id="S3.Thmremark1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\delta(t))_{t\geq 0}\in[0,+\infty[^{\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><msup><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\delta(t))_{t\geq 0}\in[0,+\infty[^{\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.Thmremark1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(t)\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(t)\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S3.Thmremark1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> (see section <a href="#S5" title="5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), we recover the convergence in <math id="S3.Thmremark1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> exactly as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p18.1" class="ltx_p">In spite of this remark, the inclusion <math id="S3.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\subset S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\subset S</annotation></semantics></math> is of importance, and will be used in our later constructions, c.f., Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 4.2. ‣ 4. Micro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S3.F3.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.15958v1/exemple_11.png" id="S3.F3.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:395/221;" width="395" height="221" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F3.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S3.F3.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Situation of Remark <a href="#S3.Thmremark1" title="Remark 3.1. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S3.F3.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.15958v1/exemple_13.png" id="S3.F3.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:296/150;" width="296" height="150" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F3.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S3.F3.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Zoom on the red square from Figure <a href="#S3.F3.sf1" title="In Figure 3 ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(a)</span></a></span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S3.F3.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.15958v1/exemple_12.png" id="S3.F3.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:296/148;" width="296" height="148" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F3.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="S3.F3.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Zoom on the blue square from Figure <a href="#S3.F3.sf1" title="In Figure 3 ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(a)</span></a></span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3. </span>Situation of Remark <a href="#S3.Thmremark1" title="Remark 3.1. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>. Figure (b) (resp (c)) is a zoom on the red (resp blue) square.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.5</span></span><span id="S3.Thmlemma5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any time <math id="S3.Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="S3.Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S3.Thmlemma5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in K</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmlemma5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.Thmlemma5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t),\partial K)\geq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t),\partial K)\geq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.Thmlemma5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}\geq 2\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{n}\delta\|x_{i}(t)\|+\frac{\alpha^{2}}{(1+\alpha)^{2}}\frac{1}{n^{2}}\delta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}\geq 2\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{n}\delta\|x_{i}(t)\|+\frac{\alpha^{2}}{(1+\alpha)^{2}}\frac{1}{n^{2}}\delta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">First of all, we claim that if <math id="S3.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)\notin K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)\notin K</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S3.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),\partial K)\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),\partial K)\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, let</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{0}\in\mathrm{argmax}_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>argmax</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{0}\in\mathrm{argmax}_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, <math id="S3.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j_{0}}(t)\notin\mbox{int}(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mtext>int</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j_{0}}(t)\notin\mbox{int}(K)</annotation></semantics></math> (because if <math id="S3.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j_{0}}(t)\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j_{0}}(t)\in K</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="S3.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> maximizes the linear function <math id="S3.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto\langle x_{i}(t),x\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto\langle x_{i}(t),x\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> over the convex set <math id="S3.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>). This also shows that the strip <math id="S3.p19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#S2.E7" title="In 2.1. Motivations ‣ 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), cannot be strictly included in <math id="S3.p19.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. Since this strip is of width <math id="S3.p19.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that either <math id="S3.p19.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)\notin K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)\notin K</annotation></semantics></math>, or</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)\in Z_{i}(t)\implies\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),\partial K)\leq\delta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)\in Z_{i}(t)\implies\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),\partial K)\leq\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p19.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p19.3.1" class="ltx_text">proving our claim.
We now rewrite</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex26X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex26X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}=2\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}=2\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex26X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex26Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex26Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\Big\|\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\Big\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\Big\|\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\Big\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p19.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p19.4.1" class="ltx_text">Note that, using the observation above, <math id="S3.p19.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\rangle\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\rangle\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, we assumed that <math id="S3.p19.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t),\partial K)\geq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t),\partial K)\geq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, hence, for any <math id="S3.p19.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p19.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)\rangle\geq\langle x_{i}(t),x_{i}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)\rangle\geq\langle x_{i}(t),x_{i}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\sum_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\|\geq\sum_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\frac{\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\rangle}{\|x_{i}(t)\|}\geq\frac{1}{\|x_{i}(t)\|}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j_{0}}(t)-x_{i}(t)\rangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\sum_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\|\geq\sum_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\frac{\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\rangle}{\|x_{i}(t)\|}\geq\frac{1}{\|x_{i}(t)\|}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j_{0}}(t)-x_{i}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p19.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p19.5.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="S3.E22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E22X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(22)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E22X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E22X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 2\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{n}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j_{0}}(t)-x_{i}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 2\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{n}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j_{0}}(t)-x_{i}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E22Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E22Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{\alpha^{2}}{(1+\alpha)^{2}}\frac{1}{n^{2}}\frac{1}{\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j_{0}}(t)-x_{i}(t)\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{\alpha^{2}}{(1+\alpha)^{2}}\frac{1}{n^{2}}\frac{1}{\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j_{0}}(t)-x_{i}(t)\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E22Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E22Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 2\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{n}\delta\|x_{i}(t)\|+\frac{\alpha^{2}}{(1+\alpha)^{2}}\frac{1}{n^{2}}\delta^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 2\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{n}\delta\|x_{i}(t)\|+\frac{\alpha^{2}}{(1+\alpha)^{2}}\frac{1}{n^{2}}\delta^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p19.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p19.6.1" class="ltx_text">This yields the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nu=\frac{\alpha^{2}}{(1+\alpha)^{2}}\frac{1}{n^{2}}\delta^{2},\quad M:=\max_{\ell\in[n]}\|x_{\ell}\|_{L^{\infty}},\quad\mathrm{and}\quad m:=\min_{\ell\in[n]}\|x_{\ell}(0)\|\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>:=</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>and</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>:=</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.059em">∥</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu=\frac{\alpha^{2}}{(1+\alpha)^{2}}\frac{1}{n^{2}}\delta^{2},\quad M:=\max_{\ell\in[n]}\|x_{\ell}\|_{L^{\infty}},\quad\mathrm{and}\quad m:=\min_{\ell\in[n]}\|x_{\ell}(0)\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmproposition1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmproposition1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmproposition1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that the following assumptions holds true:</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I7" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\in K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(0,\partial K)\geq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(0,\partial K)\geq\delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The initial tokens are all non zero;</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S3.Thmproposition1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmproposition1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, for any <math id="S3.Thmproposition1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmproposition1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq t_{\textup{lim}}:=\lfloor\frac{2c^{\star}(M+\nu)}{m\nu}\rfloor+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>lim</mtext></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq t_{\textup{lim}}:=\lfloor\frac{2c^{\star}(M+\nu)}{m\nu}\rfloor+1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="S3.Thmproposition1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(t)\|&gt;c^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(t)\|&gt;c^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> where</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="c^{\star}:=\sup\{c&gt;0\;|\;\mathrm{dist}(x,\partial K)\geq\delta\quad\forall x\in K\cap B(0,c)\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false" lspace="0.280em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>dist</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo>∂</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\star}:=\sup\{c&gt;0\;|\;\mathrm{dist}(x,\partial K)\geq\delta\quad\forall x\in K\cap B(0,c)\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.9" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, note that by our assumption (3), <math id="S3.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>, we know that any particle <math id="S3.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in B(0,c^{\star})\backslash\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in B(0,c^{\star})\backslash\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="S3.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}\geq\frac{\alpha^{2}}{(1+\alpha)^{2}}\frac{1}{n^{2}}\delta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}\geq\frac{\alpha^{2}}{(1+\alpha)^{2}}\frac{1}{n^{2}}\delta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore :</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex30X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex30X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|x_{i}(t+1)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|x_{i}(t+1)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex30X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\|x_{i}(t)\|\sqrt{1+\frac{\nu}{\|x_{i}(t)\|}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\|x_{i}(t)\|\sqrt{1+\frac{\nu}{\|x_{i}(t)\|}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex30Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex30Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\|x_{i}(t)\|\sqrt{1+\frac{\nu}{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ν</mi><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\|x_{i}(t)\|\sqrt{1+\frac{\nu}{M}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex30Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex30Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\|x_{i}(t)\|\left(1+\frac{1}{2}\frac{\nu}{M+\nu}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\|x_{i}(t)\|\left(1+\frac{1}{2}\frac{\nu}{M+\nu}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex30Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex30Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\|x_{i}(t)\|+\frac{1}{2}\frac{m\nu}{M+\nu}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\|x_{i}(t)\|+\frac{1}{2}\frac{m\nu}{M+\nu}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p20.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p20.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, for <math id="S3.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq t_{\textup{lim}}=\lfloor\frac{2c^{\star}(M+\nu)}{m\nu}\rfloor+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>lim</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq t_{\textup{lim}}=\lfloor\frac{2c^{\star}(M+\nu)}{m\nu}\rfloor+1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="S3.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(t)\|&gt;c^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(t)\|&gt;c^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.p20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, as claimed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4. </span>Micro-level properties of the trajectories</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the last section, we made an important observation that the maximal alignment set of (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) does not fully characterize where the tokens eventually converge to. This motivates further micro-level studies to gain insights about the behavior of the trajectories of the tokens in regions near the vertices of <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, we are interested in capturing an invariance-type property which we precisely define next.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="S4.Thmdefinition1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Quiescent sets):</span>

We say that a set <math id="S4.Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W\subset\real^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\subset\real^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <em id="S4.Thmdefinition1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">quiescent set</em> for the dynamics (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) if there exists a finite time <math id="S4.Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that, if token <math id="S4.Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(T)\in W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(T)\in W</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in W</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T</annotation></semantics></math>, and vice versa,
if token <math id="S4.Thmdefinition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(T)\notin W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(T)\notin W</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.Thmdefinition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\notin W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\notin W</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.Thmdefinition1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, we refer to <math id="S4.Thmdefinition1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> as the <em id="S4.Thmdefinition1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">settling time</em> for the quiescent set <math id="S4.Thmdefinition1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this sense, the set of tokens in a quiescent set for the dynamics eventually will become invariant with time. Let us note that since there is only a finite number of particles, the reciprocal statement in Definition <a href="#S4.Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 4.1. ‣ 4. Micro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> is redundant. We let it as is for clarity. We now state our main result in this section.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Quiescent sets near vertices of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>):</span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">

For <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V\backslash\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V\backslash\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\frac{\delta}{2+2\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\frac{\delta}{2+2\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> is the alignment sensitivity parameter, the set <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> is a quiescent set for the dynamics (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). Moreover, there exists a settling time <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that any token in <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> after <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> converges to <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> with a geometric rate.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of this result is involved and relies on several intermediate steps, which we develop next.
From now on, for any <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math>, we will refer to the set</p>
<table id="S4.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(23)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{v}(t):=\{x\in K_{\eta(t)}\;|\;\langle v-x_{i}(t),v\rangle\leq\delta\|v\|\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{v}(t):=\{x\in K_{\eta(t)}\;|\;\langle v-x_{i}(t),v\rangle\leq\delta\|v\|\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">as the <span id="S4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">zone of influence of <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math></span>. This name is motivated by the fact that if a particle is located in the geometric position <math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="S4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, then it will be influenced by all the particles located in <math id="S4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{v}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{v}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Our first result, roughly speaking, states that for <math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> large enough, a particle cannot move from outside of <math id="S4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{v}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{v}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> to inside <math id="S4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> in just one iteration.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\frac{\delta}{1+\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\frac{\delta}{1+\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists a time <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for any <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V\backslash\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V\backslash\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math>, any <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T</annotation></semantics></math>, and any <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v-x_{i}(t),v\rangle\geq\delta\|v\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v-x_{i}(t),v\rangle\geq\delta\|v\|</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(t+1)-v\|&gt;\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(t+1)-v\|&gt;\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">We proceed by contradiction. Suppose we can find a vertex <math id="S4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> particle <math id="S4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying :</span></p>
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v-x_{i}(t),v\rangle\geq\delta\|v\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v-x_{i}(t),v\rangle\geq\delta\|v\|</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(t+1)-v\|\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(t+1)-v\|\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S4.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="S4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> arbitrarily large. 
<br class="ltx_break">Then we can write :</span></p>
<table id="S4.E24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E24X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(24)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E24X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle x_{i}(t+1)-x_{i}(t),v\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle x_{i}(t+1)-x_{i}(t),v\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E24X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle x_{i}(t+1)-v,v\rangle+\langle v-x_{i}(t),v\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle x_{i}(t+1)-v,v\rangle+\langle v-x_{i}(t),v\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E24Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E24Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(\delta-\varepsilon)\|v\|\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(\delta-\varepsilon)\|v\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">But we also have :</span></p>
<table id="S4.E25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E25X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(25)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle x_{i}(t+1)-x_{i}(t),v\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle x_{i}(t+1)-x_{i}(t),v\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),v\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),v\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E25Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\max_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),v\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\max_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t),v\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E25Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}(\delta+\eta(t))\|v\|\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}(\delta+\eta(t))\|v\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">The last inequality holds thanks to Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, item 3. Indeed, since for any <math id="S4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)\in K_{\eta(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)\in K_{\eta(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="S4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(t)\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(t)\in K</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{j}(t)-p(t)\|\leq\eta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{j}(t)-p(t)\|\leq\eta(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex31X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex31X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle x_{j}(t)-v,v\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle x_{j}(t)-v,v\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex31X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle x_{j}(t)-p(t),v\rangle+\langle p(t)-v,v\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle x_{j}(t)-p(t),v\rangle+\langle p(t)-v,v\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex31Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex31Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\eta(t)\|v\|+\langle p(t),v\rangle-\max_{x\in K}\langle x,v\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\eta(t)\|v\|+\langle p(t),v\rangle-\max_{x\in K}\langle x,v\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex31Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex31Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\eta(t)\|v\|\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\eta(t)\|v\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p5.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.7.1" class="ltx_text">Combining equations (<a href="#S4.E24" title="In Proof. ‣ 4. Micro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E25" title="In Proof. ‣ 4. Micro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>), we get</span></p>
<table id="S4.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(26)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\delta-\alpha\eta(t)}{1+\alpha}\leq\varepsilon\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\delta-\alpha\eta(t)}{1+\alpha}\leq\varepsilon\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p5.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.8.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t)\longrightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t)\longrightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S4.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\rightarrow+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\rightarrow+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, if there exists an unbounded sequence of time such that (<a href="#S4.E26" title="In Proof. ‣ 4. Micro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) holds, we would have <math id="S4.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\geq\frac{\delta}{1+\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\geq\frac{\delta}{1+\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> which contradicts our assumption. Therefore, there exists <math id="S4.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\varepsilon)\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\varepsilon)\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> after which (<a href="#S4.E26" title="In Proof. ‣ 4. Micro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) does not hold which conclude the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Our next result states that, for <math id="S4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> large enough, the only particles in the zone of influence of <math id="S4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> must be close to <math id="S4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V\backslash\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V\backslash\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;c&lt;\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;c&lt;\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists a time <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for any <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v,v-x_{i}(t)\rangle\leq(\delta-c)\lVert v\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v,v-x_{i}(t)\rangle\leq(\delta-c)\lVert v\rVert</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert x_{i}(t)-v\rVert\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert x_{i}(t)-v\rVert\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose that we can find arbitrarily large time <math id="S4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v,v-x_{i}(t)\rangle\leq(\delta-c)\lVert v\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v,v-x_{i}(t)\rangle\leq(\delta-c)\lVert v\rVert</annotation></semantics></math>. We want to prove that this implies that <math id="S4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> influences any particle close enough to <math id="S4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle d_{\textup{min}}=\min_{w\in V\backslash\{0\}}\|w\|&gt;0,\quad d_{\textup{max}}=\max_{w\in V}\|v_{k}\|,\quad\text{and}\quad M=\max_{\ell\in[n]}\|x_{\ell}\|_{L^{\infty}}&lt;+\infty\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{\textup{min}}=\min_{w\in V\backslash\{0\}}\|w\|&gt;0,\quad d_{\textup{max}}=\max_{w\in V}\|v_{k}\|,\quad\text{and}\quad M=\max_{\ell\in[n]}\|x_{\ell}\|_{L^{\infty}}&lt;+\infty\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">We also define</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\mu\leq\min\left(c,\frac{d_{\textup{min}}}{2}\right)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\mu\leq\min\left(c,\frac{d_{\textup{min}}}{2}\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t)\leq\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t)\leq\mu</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S4.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T</annotation></semantics></math>. We claim that for any <math id="S4.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v,v-x_{i}(t)\rangle\leq(\delta-c)\lVert v\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v,v-x_{i}(t)\rangle\leq(\delta-c)\lVert v\rVert</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> influences every particle in <math id="S4.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\mu)</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, if <math id="S4.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)\in B(v,\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)\in B(v,\mu)</annotation></semantics></math>, then the assumption on <math id="S4.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> gives that <math id="S4.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{j}(t)\|\geq\frac{d_{\textup{min}}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{j}(t)\|\geq\frac{d_{\textup{min}}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and using Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 3.4. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> and Cauchy-Schwartz inequality, we have that</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex34X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex34X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{j}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{j}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex34X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\langle x_{j}(t),x_{i}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\langle x_{j}(t),x_{i}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex34Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex34Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\eta(t)\|x_{j}(t)\|+\max_{k\in[r]}\langle x_{j}(t),v_{k}\rangle-\langle x_{j}(t),x_{i}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\eta(t)\|x_{j}(t)\|+\max_{k\in[r]}\langle x_{j}(t),v_{k}\rangle-\langle x_{j}(t),x_{i}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex34Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex34Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mu\|x_{j}(t)\|+\mu\cdot d_{\textup{max}}+\mu\cdot\|x_{i}(t)\|+\max_{k\in[r]}\langle v,v_{k}\rangle-\langle v,x_{i}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mu\|x_{j}(t)\|+\mu\cdot d_{\textup{max}}+\mu\cdot\|x_{i}(t)\|+\max_{k\in[r]}\langle v,v_{k}\rangle-\langle v,x_{i}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex34Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex34Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mu\|x_{j}(t)\|+\mu\left(d_{\textup{max}}+M\right)+\langle v,v-x_{i}(t)\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mu\|x_{j}(t)\|+\mu\left(d_{\textup{max}}+M\right)+\langle v,v-x_{i}(t)\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">The last inequality holds because we know that <math id="S4.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in S</annotation></semantics></math> (Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>). Now, we use the fact that <math id="S4.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v,v-x_{i}(t)\rangle\leq(\delta-c)\|v\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v,v-x_{i}(t)\rangle\leq(\delta-c)\|v\|</annotation></semantics></math> by assumption. It follows :</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex35X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex35X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{j}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{j}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex35X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\langle x_{j}(t),x_{i}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\langle x_{j}(t),x_{i}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex35Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex35Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mu\|x_{j}(t)\|+\mu\left(d_{\textup{max}}+M\right)+(\delta-c)(\|x_{j}(t)\|+\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mu\|x_{j}(t)\|+\mu\left(d_{\textup{max}}+M\right)+(\delta-c)(\|x_{j}(t)\|+\mu)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex35Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex35Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\delta\|x_{j}(t)\|-(c-\mu)\|x_{j}(t)\|+\mu\left(d_{\textup{max}}+M\right)+(\delta-c)\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\delta\|x_{j}(t)\|-(c-\mu)\|x_{j}(t)\|+\mu\left(d_{\textup{max}}+M\right)+(\delta-c)\mu</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex35Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex35Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\delta\|x_{j}(t)\|-(c-\mu)\frac{d_{\textup{min}}}{2}+\mu\left(d_{\textup{max}}+M\right)+(\delta-c)\mu\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\delta\|x_{j}(t)\|-(c-\mu)\frac{d_{\textup{min}}}{2}+\mu\left(d_{\textup{max}}+M\right)+(\delta-c)\mu\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">Note that the quantity <math id="S4.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-(c-\mu)\frac{d_{\textup{min}}}{2}+\mu\left(d_{\textup{max}}+M\right)+(\delta-c)\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-(c-\mu)\frac{d_{\textup{min}}}{2}+\mu\left(d_{\textup{max}}+M\right)+(\delta-c)\mu</annotation></semantics></math> tends to <math id="S4.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{cd_{\textup{min}}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{cd_{\textup{min}}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S4.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, there exists <math id="S4.p7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that if <math id="S4.p7.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\mu\leq\mu_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\mu\leq\mu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p7.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is such that <math id="S4.p7.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t)\leq\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t)\leq\mu</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.p7.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.p7.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{j}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle-\langle x_{j}(t),x_{i}(t)\rangle\leq\delta\|x_{j}(t)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{j}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle-\langle x_{j}(t),x_{i}(t)\rangle\leq\delta\|x_{j}(t)\|</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S4.p7.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, <math id="S4.p7.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in C_{j}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in C_{j}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S4.p7.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S4.p7.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on the fixed parameters <math id="S4.p7.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textup{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textup{min}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p7.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textup{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textup{max}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p7.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p7.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p7.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall now the dynamics:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(27)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t+1)-x_{j}(t)=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{j}^{\delta}(t)|}\left(x_{i}(t)-x_{j}(t)+\sum_{k\in C_{j}^{\delta}(t)\backslash\{i\}}(x_{k}(t)-x_{j}(t))\right)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t+1)-x_{j}(t)=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{j}^{\delta}(t)|}\left(x_{i}(t)-x_{j}(t)+\sum_{k\in C_{j}^{\delta}(t)\backslash\{i\}}(x_{k}(t)-x_{j}(t))\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose by way of contradiction that <math id="S4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(t)-v\|\geq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(t)-v\|\geq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
We define the unit vector <math id="S4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{n}=\frac{x_{i}(t)-v}{\|x_{i}(t)-v\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{n}=\frac{x_{i}(t)-v}{\|x_{i}(t)-v\|}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have : <math id="S4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}(t)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle\geq\varepsilon-\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}(t)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle\geq\varepsilon-\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{k}(t)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle\geq-2\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{k}(t)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle\geq-2\mu</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S4.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in C_{j}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in C_{j}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore :</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex36X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex36X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|x_{j}(t+1)-x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|x_{j}(t+1)-x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex36X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(t)\|^{2}\geq\langle x_{j}(t+1)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≥</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(t)\|^{2}\geq\langle x_{j}(t+1)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex36Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex36Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{j}^{\delta}(t)|}\left(\langle x_{i}(t)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle+\sum_{k\in C_{j}^{\delta}(t)\backslash\{i\}}\langle x_{k}(t)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{j}^{\delta}(t)|}\left(\langle x_{i}(t)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle+\sum_{k\in C_{j}^{\delta}(t)\backslash\{i\}}\langle x_{k}(t)-x_{j}(t),\mathbf{n}\rangle\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex36Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex36Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{n}\left(\varepsilon-\mu-2(n-1)\mu\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{n}\left(\varepsilon-\mu-2(n-1)\mu\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Again, as <math id="S4.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the last term tends to <math id="S4.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{\varepsilon}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{\varepsilon}{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, there exists <math id="S4.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\mu_{1}&lt;\mu_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\mu_{1}&lt;\mu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> such that if <math id="S4.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is such that <math id="S4.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t)\leq\mu_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t)\leq\mu_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(t+1)-x_{i}(t)\|^{2}\geq 2\mu_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(t+1)-x_{i}(t)\|^{2}\geq 2\mu_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that <math id="S4.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> leaves the <math id="S4.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu-</annotation></semantics></math>neighborhood of <math id="S4.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="S4.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that this is true for any particle located in <math id="S4.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="S4.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T</annotation></semantics></math>. However, Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> implies that this is impossible.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We are now in a position to prove Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4. Micro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4. Micro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S4.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We divide the proof into three parts; a rough description is added to help guide the reader:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Particles outside cannot enter <math id="S4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>:<span id="S4.p11.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> This follows from Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4. Micro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.
Note that the assumption made on <math id="S4.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\leq\frac{\delta}{2+2\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\leq\frac{\delta}{2+2\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. The reason is that we can make the same reasoning as in Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4. Micro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> but with <math id="S4.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq\frac{\delta}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq\frac{\delta}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="S4.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, with this choice of <math id="S4.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S4.p11.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert x_{i}(t)-v\|\geq\frac{\delta}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≥</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert x_{i}(t)-v\|\geq\frac{\delta}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert x_{i}(t+1)-v\rVert&gt;\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">&gt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert x_{i}(t+1)-v\rVert&gt;\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> larger than some <math id="S4.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. The consequence is that if there exists <math id="S4.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\leq t_{1}&lt;t_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\leq t_{1}&lt;t_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t_{1})\notin B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t_{1})\notin B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> but <math id="S4.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t_{2})\in B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t_{2})\in B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, there must exists <math id="S4.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}\leq t_{3}&lt;t_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}\leq t_{3}&lt;t_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t_{3})\in B(v,\frac{\delta}{2})\backslash B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t_{3})\in B(v,\frac{\delta}{2})\backslash B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>. This is impossible after a certain time using Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 4.2. ‣ 4. Micro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> with <math id="S4.p11.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\frac{\delta}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\frac{\delta}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Particles in <math id="S4.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> cannot leave:<span id="S4.p12.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">. This is a logical consequence of the previous item: There is only a finite number of particles and we know that after <math id="S4.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> defined in item 1, particles outside <math id="S4.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> cannot enter this set. Therefore, the process of a particle leaving <math id="S4.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> can only happens finitely many times. Upon increasing <math id="S4.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> we can suppose that no particle leave <math id="S4.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> after <math id="S4.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmsublemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_sublemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmsublemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sublemma 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmsublemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmsublemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmsublemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmsublemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="S4.Thmsublemma1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Convergence rate of token in the quiescent set is geometric:):</span><span id="S4.Thmsublemma1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">

Let <math id="S4.Thmsublemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\frac{\delta}{2+2\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\frac{\delta}{2+2\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S4.Thmsublemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V\backslash\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V\backslash\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists a time <math id="S4.Thmsublemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for any <math id="S4.Thmsublemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and for any <math id="S4.Thmsublemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.Thmsublemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S4.Thmsublemma1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.Thmsublemma1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)\in B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)\in B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.4.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows <math id="S4.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in\mathcal{A}_{v}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in\mathcal{A}_{v}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{v}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{v}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is the zone of influence of <math id="S4.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, defined in (<a href="#S4.E23" title="In 4. Micro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>). Hence, applying Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 4.2. ‣ 4. Micro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> with <math id="S4.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\delta-\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\delta-\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that for any <math id="S4.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="S4.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\xi)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\xi)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon)\backslash B(v,\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon)\backslash B(v,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math> contains no particle for any time <math id="S4.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T(\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T(\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, using similar lines of reasoning as in Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> item 3, we know that for <math id="S4.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> small enough, if <math id="S4.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{j}(t)-v\|\geq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{j}(t)-v\|\geq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.p13.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t+1)\notin B(v,\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t+1)\notin B(v,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>. Take such a <math id="S4.p13.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and consider the associated time <math id="S4.p13.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>. We also consider the time <math id="S4.p13.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in the two previous items after which the particles in <math id="S4.p13.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed (they can’t leave and no other particle can come inside). We define <math id="S4.p13.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}=\max(T_{1},T(\xi))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}=\max(T_{1},T(\xi))</annotation></semantics></math> and we claim that <math id="S4.p13.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the statement of this sublemma. Indeed, let <math id="S4.p13.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p13.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.p13.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.p13.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T(\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T(\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p13.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon)\backslash B(v,\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon)\backslash B(v,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math> contains no particle so necessarily, <math id="S4.p13.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in B(v,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, if there exists an index <math id="S4.p13.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S4.p13.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)\notin B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)\notin B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, then we would have <math id="S4.p13.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\notin B(v,\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\notin B(v,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math> which is impossible because <math id="S4.p13.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="S4.p13.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)\in B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)\in B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> which conclude the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using Sublemma <a href="#S4.Thmsublemma1" title="Sublemma 4.1. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ 4. Micro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, we can define <math id="S4.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and suppose that any particles in <math id="S4.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is influenced exactly by all the other particles in <math id="S4.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Upon applying items 1 and 2 for <math id="S4.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we suppose that <math id="S4.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is large enough so that particles in <math id="S4.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed. Let us denote by <math id="S4.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},...,x_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},...,x_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is some positive integer, the particles in <math id="S4.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let
<math id="S4.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(t)=\frac{1}{p}\sum_{j=1}^{p}x_{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(t)=\frac{1}{p}\sum_{j=1}^{p}x_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>
be the center of mass of the particles. We have that</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t+1)=\frac{1}{1+\alpha}x_{j}(t)+\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}m(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t+1)=\frac{1}{1+\alpha}x_{j}(t)+\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}m(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, <math id="S4.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(t+1)=m(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(t+1)=m(t)</annotation></semantics></math>: the center of mass is constant. As a result, we necessarily have <math id="S4.p14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(t)=v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(t)=v</annotation></semantics></math>, because we know that we can find particle arbitrarily close to <math id="S4.p14.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.p14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> large enough and <math id="S4.p14.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is constant. Now, let</span></p>
<table id="S4.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(28)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(t)=\max_{1\leq j\leq p}\lVert x_{j}(t)-m(t)\rVert." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(t)=\max_{1\leq j\leq p}\lVert x_{j}(t)-m(t)\rVert.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">It is easy to show that <math id="S4.p14.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(t+1)=\frac{1}{1+\alpha}D(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(t+1)=\frac{1}{1+\alpha}D(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, namely we have a geometric decrease of the maximal distance between the particles in <math id="S4.p14.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p14.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(t)=v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(t)=v</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p15.1" class="ltx_p">The next result is a straightforward consequence of the the geometric convergence result in Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4. Micro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>,
and in fact is similar to what is observed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, Lemma 3.1]</cite> for the dynamics (<a href="#S1.E2" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). This phenomenon distinguishes the transformer attention dynamics from classical opinion dynamics such as Hegselmann-Krause, which have finite-time convergence properties <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="S4.Thmcorollary1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Lack of finite-time convergence):</span><span id="S4.Thmcorollary1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">

If the initial distribution <math id="S4.Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i}(0))_{1\leq i\leq n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i}(0))_{1\leq i\leq n}</annotation></semantics></math> is not at equilibrium, then there is no finite time convergence for dynamics (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p16.1" class="ltx_p">We refer the reader to Section <a href="#S7" title="7. Future directions and simulations ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, where we demonstrate the results of this section through some case studies.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In that section, we consider a natural modification of the localmax dynamics (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>),</p>
<table id="S5.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(29)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}^{\delta}(t)=\{j\in[n]\;|\;\max_{k\in[n]}\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{k}(t)\rangle-\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)\rangle\leq\delta(t)\lVert Ax_{i}(t)\rVert\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}^{\delta}(t)=\{j\in[n]\;|\;\max_{k\in[n]}\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{k}(t)\rangle-\langle Ax_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)\rangle\leq\delta(t)\lVert Ax_{i}(t)\rVert\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\delta(t))_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\delta(t))_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sequence of non-negative real numbers satisfying <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(t)\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(t)\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that as <math id="S5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(t)</annotation></semantics></math> approaches zero, this dynamics recovers the one (<a href="#S1.E3" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). We prove the following result.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5.1</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="((x_{i}(t))_{i\in[n]})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">((x_{i}(t))_{i\in[n]})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence of tokens following dynamics (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) with the neighborhood defined in (<a href="#S5.E29" title="In 5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) for some arbitrary initial distribution <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i}(0))_{1\leq i\leq n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i}(0))_{1\leq i\leq n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for any <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in S</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\xrightarrow[t\rightarrow+\infty]{}w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mphantom></mphantom></munderover><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\xrightarrow[t\rightarrow+\infty]{}w</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The upshot of this result is that, in contrast to Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4. Micro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, as <math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(t)</annotation></semantics></math> becomes small, the maximal alignment set (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In Definition 3.1. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) fully characterizes where the trajectories converge to.
As the first step in the proof, we show the following result. Naturally, after adjusting the terminology, the result recovers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, Theorem 1.1]</cite> as a corollary.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.1</span></span><span id="S5.Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the set <math id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> containing all the points located at a distance of at most <math id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S5.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(30)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S_{\varepsilon}=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\exists w\in S,\;\|x-w\|\leq\varepsilon\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\varepsilon}=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\exists w\in S,\;\|x-w\|\leq\varepsilon\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and consider the dynamics (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2. New dynamics and problem statement ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>),
with the neighborhood <math id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in (<a href="#S5.E29" title="In 5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>), with <math id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(t)</annotation></semantics></math> a vanishing sequence of alignment sensitivity parameter.
There exists a constant <math id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and a time <math id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for any <math id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\notin S_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\notin S_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="S5.Thmlemma1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}\geq\gamma\varepsilon." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}\geq\gamma\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Clearly, the statement is related to the Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>, but crucially, the result is concerned with a vanishing time-varying alignment sensitivity parameter <math id="S5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, as outlined below, the proof additionally uses some results from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall from the proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> that</span></p>
<table id="S5.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(31)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}\geq 2\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\rangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}\geq 2\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{1}{|C_{i}^{\delta}(t)|}\sum_{j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">and set <math id="S5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ij}(t)=\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ij}(t)=\langle x_{i}(t),x_{j}(t)-x_{i}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. We need to find a bound on <math id="S5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ij}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ij}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. We start by fixing an <math id="S5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that all the <math id="S5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-neighborhood of points in <math id="S5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> are separated by a distance of at most <math id="S5.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we use two results from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>:</span></p>
<ol id="S5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There exists <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that, if <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K_{\lambda}\backslash S_{\varepsilon_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K_{\lambda}\backslash S_{\varepsilon_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> then, using
the proof of the first case of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, Theorem 3.1, Claim 2]</cite>,
<math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{k\in[r]}\langle x,v_{k}\rangle-\langle x,x\rangle\geq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{k\in[r]}\langle x,v_{k}\rangle-\langle x,x\rangle\geq c</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. We now define <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t)\leq\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t)\leq\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. After time <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, all the particles are in <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There exists <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K\cap B(\omega,\varepsilon_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K\cap B(\omega,\varepsilon_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, then, using <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, Lemma 8.4]</cite>,</p>
<table id="S5.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(32)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{k\in[r]}\langle x,v_{k}-x\rangle\geq\beta\|x-\omega\|\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{k\in[r]}\langle x,v_{k}-x\rangle\geq\beta\|x-\omega\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Following the same steps as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, Theorem 3.1, Claim 2]</cite>, we conclude that there exists a time <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in S_{\varepsilon_{0}}\backslash S_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in S_{\varepsilon_{0}}\backslash S_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{k\in[r]}\langle x_{i}(t),v_{k}-x_{i}(t)\rangle\geq\frac{\beta}{2}\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{k\in[r]}\langle x_{i}(t),v_{k}-x_{i}(t)\rangle\geq\frac{\beta}{2}\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S5.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, for any <math id="S5.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\frac{2c}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\frac{2c}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, any <math id="S5.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq\max(T_{1},T_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq\max(T_{1},T_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\notin S_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\notin S_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, by combining the two statements above, we have that</span></p>
<table id="S5.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(33)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{j\in[n]}a_{ij}(t)\geq\max_{k\in[r]}\langle x_{i}(t),v_{k}-x_{i}(t)\rangle\geq\tilde{\gamma}\varepsilon" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{j\in[n]}a_{ij}(t)\geq\max_{k\in[r]}\langle x_{i}(t),v_{k}-x_{i}(t)\rangle\geq\tilde{\gamma}\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="S5.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\gamma}=\frac{\beta}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\gamma}=\frac{\beta}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now define <math id="S5.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{3}\geq\max(T_{1},T_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{3}\geq\max(T_{1},T_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for any <math id="S5.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(t)&lt;\frac{\tilde{\gamma}\varepsilon}{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(t)&lt;\frac{\tilde{\gamma}\varepsilon}{M}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\max_{\ell\in[n]}\|x_{\ell}\|_{L^{\infty}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\max_{\ell\in[n]}\|x_{\ell}\|_{L^{\infty}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex38X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex38X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex38X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\iff\max_{\ell\in[n]}a_{il}(t)-a_{ij}(t)\leq\delta(t)\|x_{i}(t)\|\implies\tilde{\gamma}\varepsilon-a_{ij}(t)\leq\tilde{\gamma}\varepsilon," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iff\max_{\ell\in[n]}a_{il}(t)-a_{ij}(t)\leq\delta(t)\|x_{i}(t)\|\implies\tilde{\gamma}\varepsilon-a_{ij}(t)\leq\tilde{\gamma}\varepsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">which implies that <math id="S5.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ij}(t)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ij}(t)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="S5.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(34)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}\geq 2\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{\tilde{\gamma}\varepsilon}{n}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}\geq 2\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}\frac{\tilde{\gamma}\varepsilon}{n}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We are now able to proceed with the proof the Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1. ‣ 5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1. ‣ 5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S5.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Our goal is to prove that if <math id="S5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, all the particles are located in <math id="S5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> after a finite time (in fact, we only need to prove this for <math id="S5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> small enough). We first discuss the case where <math id="S5.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, and then treat the case where <math id="S5.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(t)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(t)\|</annotation></semantics></math> is non zero.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The case <math id="S5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\in S</annotation></semantics></math>:<span id="S5.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Let <math id="S5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. According to Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 5.1. ‣ 5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, there exists <math id="S5.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{T}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{T}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="S5.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq\tilde{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq\tilde{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="S5.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S5.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\notin B(0,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\notin B(0,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, then it will never enter it. We can therefore distinguish between particles that remain indefinitely in <math id="S5.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(0,\varepsilon)\subset S_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(0,\varepsilon)\subset S_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> for which nothing further needs to be proved, and particles that eventually leave <math id="S5.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(0,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(0,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> whose norm is then bounded below by <math id="S5.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. With this at hand, we assume from now on that <math id="S5.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(t)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(t)\|</annotation></semantics></math> is non zero. We first gather some preliminary observations:</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Preliminary results:<span id="S5.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Let <math id="S5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in S</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, <math id="S5.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle w,v_{k}\rangle=\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle w,v_{\ell}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle w,v_{k}\rangle=\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle w,v_{\ell}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S5.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathcal{I}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathcal{I}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us denote by <math id="S5.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> the face of <math id="S5.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> generated by the vertices in <math id="S5.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We define</span></span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{w}^{\varepsilon}=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\mathrm{dist}(x,F_{w})\leq\varepsilon\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{w}^{\varepsilon}=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\mathrm{dist}(x,F_{w})\leq\varepsilon\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S5.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K_{\eta(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K_{\eta(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="S5.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{x}:=\{k\in[r]\;|\;\langle x,v_{k}\rangle=\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle x,v_{\ell}\rangle\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{x}:=\{k\in[r]\;|\;\langle x,v_{k}\rangle=\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle x,v_{\ell}\rangle\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be as defined in Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>. This lemma gives that for any <math id="S5.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="S5.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in F_{w}^{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in F_{w}^{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{x}\subset\mathcal{I}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{x}\subset\mathcal{I}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> which implies that the face <math id="S5.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S5.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> generated by the vertices in <math id="S5.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is included in <math id="S5.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, for <math id="S5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K_{\eta(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K_{\eta(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the hyperplanes</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H_{1}:=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{1}:=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\langle x,y\rangle=\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle x,v_{\ell}\rangle\},\quad\mathrm{and}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>and</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\langle x,y\rangle=\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle x,v_{\ell}\rangle\},\quad\mathrm{and}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H_{2}:=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{2}:=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\langle x,y\rangle=\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle x,v_{\ell}\rangle-\delta(t)\|x\|\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\;|\;\langle x,y\rangle=\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle x,v_{\ell}\rangle-\delta(t)\|x\|\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="S5.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K_{\eta(t)}\backslash B(0,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K_{\eta(t)}\backslash B(0,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S5.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(x,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math> be the strip of width <math id="S5.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(t)</annotation></semantics></math>
delimited by the hyperplanes <math id="S5.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, <math id="S5.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is tangential to <math id="S5.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and only in <math id="S5.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="S5.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}\cap K=F_{x}\subset F_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}\cap K=F_{x}\subset F_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S5.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in F_{w}^{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in F_{w}^{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This implies that, for any <math id="S5.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
there exists <math id="S5.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(\lambda)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(\lambda)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (a scalar depending on <math id="S5.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and on the geometry of <math id="S5.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> but not on <math id="S5.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>) such that if <math id="S5.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(t)\leq a(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(t)\leq a(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>, then for any <math id="S5.p10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in F_{w}^{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in F_{w}^{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{L}(x,t)\cap K\implies\mathrm{dist}(y,F_{w})\leq\lambda." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{L}(x,t)\cap K\implies\mathrm{dist}(y,F_{w})\leq\lambda.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, there exists <math id="S5.p10.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\lambda)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\lambda)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that if <math id="S5.p10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="S5.p10.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(t)\leq a(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(t)\leq a(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and thus,</span></p>
<table id="S5.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(35)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{L}(x,t)\cap K\implies\mathrm{dist}(y,F_{w})\leq\lambda,\;\;\;\forall x\in F_{w}^{\varepsilon}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.007em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{L}(x,t)\cap K\implies\mathrm{dist}(y,F_{w})\leq\lambda,\;\;\;\forall x\in F_{w}^{\varepsilon}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, we know that if <math id="S5.p10.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in F_{w}^{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in F_{w}^{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> then</span></p>
<table id="S5.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(36)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}(t)\cap K\subset\mathcal{L}(x_{i}(t),t)\cap K." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}(t)\cap K\subset\mathcal{L}(x_{i}(t),t)\cap K.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">This is because if <math id="S5.p10.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in K</annotation></semantics></math> is such that <math id="S5.p10.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle-\langle x_{i}(t),y\rangle\leq\delta(t)\|x_{i}(t)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\ell\in[n]}\langle x_{i}(t),x_{\ell}(t)\rangle-\langle x_{i}(t),y\rangle\leq\delta(t)\|x_{i}(t)\|</annotation></semantics></math>, then using the left inequality of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 3.4. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, it follows <math id="S5.p10.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}(t),y\rangle\geq\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle x_{i}(t),v_{\ell}\rangle-\delta(t)\|x_{i}(t)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}(t),y\rangle\geq\max_{\ell\in[r]}\langle x_{i}(t),v_{\ell}\rangle-\delta(t)\|x_{i}(t)\|</annotation></semantics></math> and so <math id="S5.p10.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{L}(x_{i}(t),t)\cap K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{L}(x_{i}(t),t)\cap K</annotation></semantics></math>.
In what precedes, <math id="S5.p10.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p10.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> depend on <math id="S5.p10.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in S</annotation></semantics></math> (actually, on the local geometry of <math id="S5.p10.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> around <math id="S5.p10.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>). However, since <math id="S5.p10.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, we can assume that the same two quantities are valid for any <math id="S5.p10.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in K</annotation></semantics></math>. We fix <math id="S5.p10.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> small enough so that the previous statements hold for any <math id="S5.p10.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in S</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmsublemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_sublemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmsublemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sublemma 5.1</span></span><span id="S5.Thmsublemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmsublemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.Thmsublemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmsublemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="S5.Thmsublemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S5.Thmsublemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmsublemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in F_{w}^{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in F_{w}^{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|2\lambda-\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t),F_{w})|\to 0\quad\text{ as }\quad t\to\infty\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> as </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|2\lambda-\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t),F_{w})|\to 0\quad\text{ as }\quad t\to\infty\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Sublemma <a href="#S5.Thmsublemma1" title="Sublemma 5.1. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>:<span id="S5.p11.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Let <math id="S5.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S5.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in F_{w}^{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in F_{w}^{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> then for any <math id="S5.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S5.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)\in Z_{i}(t)\cap K_{\eta(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)\in Z_{i}(t)\cap K_{\eta(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S5.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)\in K</annotation></semantics></math> then (<a href="#S5.E36" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>) gives that <math id="S5.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)\in\mathcal{L}(x_{i}(t),t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)\in\mathcal{L}(x_{i}(t),t)</annotation></semantics></math> and (<a href="#S5.E35" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>) ensures that <math id="S5.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{dist}(x_{j}(t),F_{w})\leq\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>dist</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{dist}(x_{j}(t),F_{w})\leq\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S5.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}(t)\in Z_{i}(t)\cup K_{\eta(t)}\backslash K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}(t)\in Z_{i}(t)\cup K_{\eta(t)}\backslash K</annotation></semantics></math>, then (<a href="#S5.E36" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>) gives <math id="S5.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),\mathcal{L}(x_{i}(t),t))\leq\eta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),\mathcal{L}(x_{i}(t),t))\leq\eta(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and (<a href="#S5.E35" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>) gives <math id="S5.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),F_{w})\leq\lambda+\eta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),F_{w})\leq\lambda+\eta(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Upon increasing <math id="S5.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can assume that if <math id="S5.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t)\leq\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t)\leq\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>. To summarize, if <math id="S5.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p11.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\in F_{w}^{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\in F_{w}^{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, then for any <math id="S5.p11.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in C_{i}^{\delta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p11.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),F_{w})\leq 2\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(x_{j}(t),F_{w})\leq 2\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, which yields the claims.
 <span id="S5.p11.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><math id="S5.p11.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\diamond" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋄</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\diamond</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Main part of the proof :<span id="S5.p12.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> First, note that for any <math id="S5.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S5.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is the orthogonal projection of the origin to <math id="S5.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S5.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{y\in B(w,\varepsilon)}\|y\|^{2}=\|w\|^{2}+\varepsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{y\in B(w,\varepsilon)}\|y\|^{2}=\|w\|^{2}+\varepsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, for the same reason,</span></span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\inf\{\|x\|^{2},x\notin B(w,\varepsilon)\;\mbox{and}\;\mathrm{dist}(x,F_{w})\leq c\|w\|\}&gt;(1-c)^{2}\|w\|^{2}+\varepsilon^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>and</mtext><mi>dist</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf\{\|x\|^{2},x\notin B(w,\varepsilon)\;\mbox{and}\;\mathrm{dist}(x,F_{w})\leq c\|w\|\}&gt;(1-c)^{2}\|w\|^{2}+\varepsilon^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, if we define <math id="S5.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;z&lt;\sqrt{\gamma\varepsilon}\frac{\min_{s\in S\backslash\{0\}}\|s\|}{\max_{s\in S}\|s\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;z&lt;\sqrt{\gamma\varepsilon}\frac{\min_{s\in S\backslash\{0\}}\|s\|}{\max_{s\in S}\|s\|}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x\|^{2}+\gamma\varepsilon&gt;\sup_{y\in B(w,\varepsilon)}\|y\|^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">&gt;</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x\|^{2}+\gamma\varepsilon&gt;\sup_{y\in B(w,\varepsilon)}\|y\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">for any <math id="S5.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K\backslash S_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K\backslash S_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S5.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{dist}(x,F_{w})\leq z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>dist</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{dist}(x,F_{w})\leq z</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="S5.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in S\backslash\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in S\backslash\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 5.1. ‣ 5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, there exists a constant <math id="S5.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and a time <math id="S5.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> after which, for any <math id="S5.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S5.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\notin S_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\notin S_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="S5.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}\geq\gamma\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}\geq\gamma\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, let <math id="S5.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq\max(T_{1},T_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq\max(T_{1},T_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.p12.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in Sublemma <a href="#S5.Thmsublemma1" title="Sublemma 5.1. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> for <math id="S5.p12.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\frac{z}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>z</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\frac{z}{4}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.p12.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S5.p12.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)\notin S_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)\notin S_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 5.1. ‣ 5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> imposes that <math id="S5.p12.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}\geq\gamma\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(t+1)\|^{2}-\|x_{i}(t)\|^{2}\geq\gamma\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S5.p12.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded, the squared norm of <math id="S5.p12.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> cannot increase indefinitely, hence <math id="S5.p12.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> will reach <math id="S5.p12.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(w,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(w,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S5.p12.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in S</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="S5.p12.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{3}\geq\max(T_{1},T_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{3}\geq\max(T_{1},T_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, by the Sublemma <a href="#S5.Thmsublemma1" title="Sublemma 5.1. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, we have <math id="S5.p12.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|2\lambda-\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t),F_{w})|\xrightarrow[t\rightarrow+\infty]{}0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mphantom></mphantom></munderover><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|2\lambda-\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t),F_{w})|\xrightarrow[t\rightarrow+\infty]{}0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, there exists <math id="S5.p12.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{4}\geq T_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{4}\geq T_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S5.p12.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t),F_{w})\leq 3\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t),F_{w})\leq 3\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="S5.p12.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{4}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, if there exists <math id="S5.p12.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{5}\geq T_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{5}\geq T_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S5.p12.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(T_{5})\notin B(w,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(T_{5})\notin B(w,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, since
<math id="S5.p12.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(T_{5}),F_{w})\leq 3\lambda&lt;z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(T_{5}),F_{w})\leq 3\lambda&lt;z</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}(T_{5})\|^{2}+\gamma\varepsilon&gt;\sup_{y\in B(w,\varepsilon)}\|y\|^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">&gt;</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}(T_{5})\|^{2}+\gamma\varepsilon&gt;\sup_{y\in B(w,\varepsilon)}\|y\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p12.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p12.4.1" class="ltx_text">and Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 5.1. ‣ 5. Localmax dynamics in the vanishing alignment sensitivity regime ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> proves that <math id="S5.p12.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> will never re-enter <math id="S5.p12.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(w,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(w,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> at any time <math id="S5.p12.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="S5.p12.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> will reach the <math id="S5.p12.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-neighborhood of another point in <math id="S5.p12.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, say <math id="S5.p12.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, to which the same argument applies.
Since there is only a finite number of elements of <math id="S5.p12.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, and we have just shown that after a finite time <math id="S5.p12.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> cannot re-enter <math id="S5.p12.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-neighborhood of points in <math id="S5.p12.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> that it has already visited, this process must stop after a finite time. This means that <math id="S5.p12.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> will eventually enter the <math id="S5.p12.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-neighborhood of an element <math id="S5.p12.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in S</annotation></semantics></math> and never leave it. As the argument holds for any token <math id="S5.p12.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we have proved that after a finite time, all particles remain in <math id="S5.p12.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to prove that particles cannot “jump” infinitely often between different connected components of <math id="S5.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>. In fact, we know that after <math id="S5.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we always have <math id="S5.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t),F_{w})\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(x_{i}(t),F_{w})\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, so by Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3. Macro-level properties of the trajectories ‣ Localmax dynamics for attention in Transformers and its asymptotic behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> we can conclude that <math id="S5.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{x_{i}(t)}\subseteq F_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{x_{i}(t)}\subseteq F_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S5.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{x_{i}(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{x_{i}(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the face of <math id="S5.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> generated by the vertices maximizing the scalar product with <math id="S5.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that, after <math id="S5.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S5.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> “jumps” from <math id="S5.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(w,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(w,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(w^{\prime},\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(w^{\prime},\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.p13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}\neq w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}\neq w</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.p13.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{w^{\prime}}\subset F_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{w^{\prime}}\subset F_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>. But <math id="S5.p13.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is the point that minimizes the norm over <math id="S5.p13.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>, so it is unique and the inclusion <math id="S5.p13.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{w^{\prime}}\subset F_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{w^{\prime}}\subset F_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> is strict. Hence, the dimension of the facet <math id="S5.p13.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{w^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{w^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly less than that of <math id="S5.p13.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>. The same argument applies again if <math id="S5.p13.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> “jumps” from <math id="S5.p13.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(w^{\prime},\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(w^{\prime},\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> to another connected component of <math id="S5.p13.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>. This process must terminate once <math id="S5.p13.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> reaches <math id="S5.p13.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(v,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(v,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.p13.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inl